issing the cash? Hmm."1You've... got your own set of problems, huh?"Formation 4C, Gurdurr!"Get ready to block 'em!"$Our defensive line collapsed...">We need to hit the gym. I hope Eko is taking challengers!"Oh… you destroyed it.">I was watching that avatar, and you just… dismissed it."&Well, it couldn’t last forever."5Nice to meet you. My name’s <imp>Skyler</imp>."OYou were superb, by the way. Fought like the sun against the morning mist."KAnd, I suppose I can’t complain. I can leave now, at the very least."Skyler."vI don’t know what else you want me to say. I’m a traveler on a pilgrimage of sorts, which I can now continue.""All thanks to you, of course."EI’d opted to take a short nap before continuing my pilgrimage."YHah. Bit of a mistake. The avatar showed up while I was sleeping, not that I minded."vMakya’s a beautiful region, full of beautiful people. But I’m going to admit that I’m here for the avatars."aEveryone’s concerned with how dangerous they are, but I think they’re missing the point."pWe’ve gotten jaded. Pokémon used to be magical. We used to worship them. I think we’ve forgotten that."%So are you! Look how you fought!"mBut I’m interested in you nonetheless. Call it a dangerous obsession or a leap of faith – your pick."[But were they always? You’ve heard legends of Pokémon raising mountains and oceans."IWe were created by Pokémon, and they’ll be the end of us someday."YAt least, that’s what they say of Arceus and Yveltal, not to mention all the rest.""I’m glad to hear you agree."pMaybe it’s a foolish endeavor, seeking these things out. I’m sure they’d maul me given half a chance."BBut maybe reverence, not fear, is what they’re looking for."LIn any case, I’m glad I met you. Technically, I suppose you saved me."LI’ll be back on my little journey now, but, uh, I’ll see you again."pA trainer like you must be seeking badges, right? So let’s meet in the <imp>town ruined by avatars</imp>."NI hear there’s a gym leader there. So long, my knight in shining ar