't pay me any mind."OI'm just here to discuss some possible changes to the monument with Jovan."You've met, I believe?"/I'll take your Pokémon for a few seconds."<First, you should restore your Pokémon to full health."We hope you excel!"-Offensive Pokémon need offensive moves."9Most of the time you’ve got more moves than types."lThat means you’re going to want some attacking moves that complement the moves that match your types."%Think long and hard about those."4A Normal-type might want a Dark or Ground move."cIf your team’s weak to Ice, maybe here’s where you slip in a Mach Punch or a Flamethrower."Think about it."MHeyo, \PN. Want some guaranteed one-hundred-percent success rate advice?"NNever be afraid to bring, like, five Pokémon that all do the same thing."&They can’t counter all of them."iNo, but seriously, doubling or tripling or quadrupling down can overwhelm your opponent’s answers."1How many Water resists can they really have?"pAnd, hey, if you’ve got a spare team slot, bring something hyper-focused on countering what counters you."UAww. Well, at least read what I’ve written. It’s up on one of the computers."\PN! Nice to see you."qI mean, you're the champion, now, so I suppose it's only natural that you'd try take on the Battle Monument."aI did some consulting work on the trainer AI, so I'm very aware that it's quite a challenge."Good luck!"Champion. Good seeing you."Do you need some advice?"�Take a second draft. Running your team into the Monument without hours of research can feel like feeding them into a meat grinder.">But don’t discount the value of practice and iteration."-Take note of what you couldn’t answer."PEven swapping out a few moves or items can make a night-and-day difference."YEven the most hopeless of teams can be honed into something usable with enough work."CGood to hear! I’ll refrain from wishing you good luck, then."OIf said luck does begin to turn, though, I encourage you to read my guide."'It’s up on one of the computers."
