Yeah."Not really.[7"8装饰起来！每只精灵都需要一个物品！"e如果你拿不定主意，给它们剩饭或闪亮的新宝石，然后看它们大显身手。"V有几十种物品可供选择，我相信你能找到适合你精灵的东西！"S用龙舞之类的技能强化，可以把精灵变成不可阻挡的巨兽。",但要耐心。选对时机和地点。"V等到你能安全强化的机会，并确保没有意外的威胁在等着你。")记得在战斗中查看信息栏。">它会告诉你对手（或你自身）的详细数据。"J你也可以查看大师图鉴，了解对手可能学会的技能。"A否则，你可能会在吃亏后才发现对手会冰砾。"n而且，嘿，你可以在战斗后用大师图鉴寻找潜在的队伍成员。只需筛选和搜索。"又见面了，冠军。"别管我。"D我只是来和约凡讨论纪念碑的一些可能的改动。"你们见过，对吧？",请允许我暂时拿走您的精灵。"/现在你的精灵已经恢复活力了。"祝您一路顺风！",攻击型精灵需要伤害类技能。"2大多数时候，你的技能比属性多。"S这意味着你需要一些伤害类技能来补充与属性匹配的技能。"仔细考虑这些。"G一半属性精灵可能会想要恶属性或地面属性技能。"V如果你的队伍弱冰，也许可以在这里加入音速拳或喷射火焰。"好好想想。"J嘿哟，\PN。想要一些保证百分之百成功率的建议吗？"0别害怕带上5只功能相同的精灵。"#他们不可能全部防住。"Y不，说真的，2倍、3倍甚至4倍的投入可以压倒对手的应对手段。"5他们真的能有那么多抗水的精灵吗？"\而且，如果你有空余的队伍位置，带一些专门针对你弱点的精灵。"J啊，好吧，至少读读我写的东西。它在一台电脑上。" \PN！能见到你真好。"h我是说，你现在已经是冠军了，所以想要挑战对战纪念碑也是理所当然的。"a我在训练师AI方面做过一些咨询工作，所以我很清楚这相当有挑战性。"祝你好运！"#冠军，很高兴见到你。" 你需要一些建议吗？"q再考虑一下。不经过充分研究就把队伍带进纪念碑，感觉就像把它们送进绞肉机。"/但不要忽视练习和调整的价值。"&记下你无法应对的情况。"J即使只是更换几个技能或物品，也能带来天壤之别。"M即使是最无望的队伍，经过足够的努力也能变得可用。">很高兴听你这么说！那我就不祝你好运了。"J但如果运气真的开始变差，我建议你读读我的指南。"它在一台电脑上。"确定吗？"不了，谢谢。"是的。"不太需要。;[7"/Accessorize! Every Pokémon NEEDS an item!"dIf you can’t decide, give them Leftovers or a shiny new Gem and watch them strut their stuff."tThere are dozens and dozens of items to pick from, so I’m sure you can find something to match your Pokémon!"dSetting up with something like Dragon Dance can turn a Pokémon into an unstoppable juggernaut."3But be patient. Pick the right time and place."|Wait for something you can set up on without being humbled, and make sure there’s no nasty surprises waiting in the wings.".Remember to check the Info tab in battle."QThat’ll give you the nitty-gritty on your opponent’s stats – or yours."VYou can also check the MasterDex to see what kinds of moves your opponent learns."JOtherwise you might find out something learns Ice Shard the hard way."eAnd, hey, you can use it after the fight to find potential team members. Just filter and search."Hello again, champion."Don't pay me any mind."OI'm just here to discuss some possible changes to the monument with Jovan."You've met, I believe?"/I'll take your Pokémon for a few seconds."<First, you should restore your Pokémon to full health."We hope you excel!"-Offensive Pokémon need offensive moves."9Most of the time you’ve got more moves than types."lThat means you’re going to want some attacking moves that complement the moves that match your types."%Think long and hard about those."4A Normal-type might want a Dark or Ground move."cIf your team’s weak to Ice, maybe here’s where you slip in a Mach Punch or a Flamethrower."Think about it."MHeyo, \PN. Want some guaranteed one-hundred-percent success rate advice?"NNever be afraid to bring, like, five Pokémon that all do the same thing."&They can’t counter all of them."iNo, but seriously, doubling or tripling or quadrupling down can overwhelm your opponent’s answers."1How many Water resists can they really have?"pAnd, hey, if you’ve got a spare team slot, bring something hyper-focused on countering what counters you."UAww. Well, at least read what I’ve written. It’s up on one of the computers."\PN! Nice to see you."qI mean, you're the champion, now, so I suppose it's only natural that you'd try take on the Battle Monument."aI did some consulting work on the trainer AI, so I'm very aware that it's quite a challenge."Good luck!"Champion. Good seeing you."Do you need some advice?"�Take a second draft. Running your team into the Monument without hours of research can feel like feeding them into a meat grinder.">But don’t discount the value of practice and iteration."-Take note of what you couldn’t answer."PEven swapping out a few moves or items can make a night-and-day difference."YEven the most hopeless of teams can be honed into something usable with enough work."CGood to hear! I’ll refrain from wishing you good luck, then."OIf said luck does begin to turn, though, I encourage you to read my guide."'It’s up on one of the computers."
