l of this! This entire place is mega-screwed because of what she did!",Eh! No! No talking! I can’t hear you!"}I am one hundred percent not interested in, like, anything you’re saying. I trust you. I trust you, and that’s that."lSo you go in and I’ll scoot ‘round the back, and we’ll do a pincer maneuver, alright? Let’s go!"West: Eleig River Crossing"East: Canal Desert"UI've been managing the wildlife here for years, I've become an honorary Bibarel!"aWhoa! That last move almost smashed the whole dam! I'll get right back to work fixing it up!"aAnother day, another trainer recklessly battled on this new dam. My Pokemon love the thrill!"?This is such a nice spot, I should bring a couch out here."kUsed to look a little more pretty before the Biberal cut down the trees, but I appreciate the company."Um... hey."9So, Tamarind and I, like, kissed and made up? Kinda?"GUm, not in that way. She’s like twenty-five years older than me."@I... \PN, I still really hate her. She is, like, the worst."�She’s this snooty arrogant brat that literally destroys things that get in her way for no reason. But, like, I can’t just punch her and make it better."...But I did punch her."ENot really! It was kind of a wimpy punch. Still, I had to do it."For baby Candy, at least."#I know, I know! It was stupid."VBut, like, I’ve thought about it so many times, and now I finally got to do it."LIt didn’t make me happy, but I can scratch it off the list, y’know?"DOh, not even. She deserves to be punched, like, at least twice."6What? That punching her doesn’t make it better?"hOr that I, like, decked her in the first place? Because the answer is yeah, I’m a learning Candy."HReally, I let her off easy. But, um, I didn’t really let her off."sI kinda... got hired? Like, I do not trust that hag for a second, so I’m gonna stick to her like a Remoraid."OShe’s gonna fix all the messed-up stuff that she and her cronies caused."OAnd she’s, like, totally overworked, so, um... yeah. I’m her aide now!"#And bodyguard. And conscience."WI get to get justice, and she gets to not have her labs be on fire. Everyone wins."@Heh… thanks. I’m, like, not sure of anything right now."VWho knows! Maybe I’ll think better of it tomorrow and firebomb her lab anyways!")Hey! What’s that supposed to mean?"UDo you think I’m just, like, this belligerent ditzy manic Spritzee dream girl?"]No, but, yeah, I get it. I don’t know that I’m, like, super cut out for this either."=Um. I think, like, you can get fired for that? So... no?""Maybe. I’ll think about it."uWell, now if I want to steal someone’s Pokémon back I can just have Tamarind order it, so, like, I guess not?"kI’m still gonna steal things. Let’s all be, like, honest for a second: I’m not changing my ways."MBut I am gonna be busier with other stuff now! So, yeah. There’s that."+Oh, by the way, Tamarind was all like:"�“If you want proof that I’m doing my damnedest to help this region” and then she blabbered about like a secret lab and horrible monsters."�Y’know. Like, containing an extradimensional evil and all that. Anyways, she gave me this key, but I don’t really, like, care?"�Like, sure, whatever, she did hard work. She wants to prove she’s good, she can put her money where her mouth is and prove it by working with me."SAnyways, um… you can have it? Maybe cool stuff? Maybe extradimensional evil?"$Um, anyways, yeah. I, um, yeah."Thanks."1Thanks, like, a lot. You’re a good friend.""But, um, I think that’s it."{I have to go with Tamarind now and make sure she doesn’t, like, kick a child or something on the way back to Prizca.">So, this is goodbye. And, well, you know what that means."E*sniff* Yeah... aww, \PN, we can’t be justice friends anymore."%We’ll just be regular friends."wI’m gonna see you again, I know, but… we had like an arc together! We had an arc, and now it’s over. *sniff*"{Aww, don’t tempt me. But, um, I kinda had my Pokémon tussle with Tamarind back there and they need to rest for now."2Maybe someday? Jeanne wants to kick 