stice is."=...Ugh, that was cheesy. I, um, yeah. Love you. Toodles."7You’re cool. You’re, like, my favorite person."HI know you’ve still got, like, a lot of stuff to do, so go do it."`I’ve got stuff to do, too. If Tamarind wasn’t waiting I’d, like, hug you for an hour."jBut, um, gotta go, I guess. You’re... we’ll see each other again? Right? Yeah. Of course we will.")I, um, yeah. Love you. Bye. Toodles!"KOh, so it’s you again. You’ve arrived at a rather fortuitous time."pI’ve caught this pair of Makyan forms and would like some more data – but excuse me. Again, my manners."May I ask your name?"VAh, \PN. I’ve heard that name about. A pleasure to meet you properly this time."=How droll. I suppose I am a stranger, after all, though."`As I was saying: I would like some combat data. You seem to be quite adept at providing it."Shall we?"<Of course. I wouldn’t want the results to be tainted."JAdaptation via vendetta – I’m expecting viciousness. Let’s see."Shall we get down to it?"Highly educational."GIt would seem that both of them have been honed by their vendetta."dFrom what I’ve gleaned in local sources, the Sevipers became Steel-type to fend off Zangoose."nThey managed to drive the local Zangoose populations to extinction, yet even that didn’t stop the feud."cFighting until they died, and then even beyond. The tenacity of the Zangoose is admirable, no?"tThe Zangoose counter-adaptation – the Fighting-type – seems to be a product of their indestructible spirit."GCurious. Could these be the predators the Furrets adapted to beat?"5No, the Psychic type would hurt as much as help."nA mystery for another time. I would like to thank you for your help, but actions speak louder than words."!Take this, from my homeland."5Goodbye. I can’t say where I’ll end up next."rPerhaps the <imp>sewers beneath Prizca</imp>. If any biome might cause new forms to emerge, it would be that.".The Saurenaid is humming a pleasant tune."?It's strapped up with multiple cushioned seats for travel."