 few Trainers."!The door is securely locked."IThe spine of "Makyan Battle Policies: Volume II" is heavily creased."Capitol Library"Press Room"I worry about my grandson.":He works at the castle on the north side of the city."jHe always gets involved with dangerous Pokemon, and I'm not just talking about the avatars he fights."OIt always looks like he's a breeze away from being caught in the blasts..."DThe avatar crisis is really starting to threaten our wellbeing."nIf it weren't for the Rangers and their volunteers, avatars would probably be causing irreparable damage."aThe sign lists off rules you have to follow to schedule meetings with Members of Parliament."gThe poster details which regions allow trainers to use Makyan Pokémon in league-official battles."7Hey kid, I'm gonna have to ask you to take a seat."&You can ask your questions later."Ma'am, if you would!"FAvatars have already destroyed the bridge across the Eleig River."iCoupled with the incident at Velenz, how can people be confident that Makya is a safe place to live?"BA view of the Eleig river from a quiet vantage point in town.",Are you scheduled to speak later today?"ONo? Then I'm gonna have to ask you to find a spot to watch the conference."JI work here in the capitol building, recording meetings and the like."6But I really want to be a documentary film-maker!"*I have my subject already picked out."4There's this girl who is friends with everyone."5Wherever I go in Makya, I keep hearing her name."Hearing her name."Lainie."..."6...huh? What are you staring at me like that for?")You're creeping me out, I'm leaving.".You wait for a representative to show up."Looks like nobody's free."[I've lived a life of luxury, in no small part due to my lucrative career as a Trainer.">I managed to get my hands on a few of these Amulet Coins.".They made me a fortune in no time at all."XBut now I have a nice place for myself here. It pays well and it's easy on my body."@I don't really need these anymore, so I'll 