der the burners."1The thought of touching it makes you queasy.""Full of old cans and bottles."HOh. Hello. You’ve caught me at the absolute worst time, you know?";I’m technically breaking and entering at the moment.">This used to be a cozy little restaurant run by a friend."yShe bought the place, remodeled it so she could cook on the first floor and live on the second, and now it’s this."Empty."sOh, it’s not so bad. Everything has its season, and in Makya it’s barely summer a day before winter comes.""Constant tumult, this region."DI didn’t believe it at first. That she’d just up and leave."RI figured I was always welcome here anyways, and I know my way around a lock."Eternally, my savior."`And if that flattery isn’t enough for you, I WAS trying to find another way to repay you."HUnfortunately, dinner seems to be off the table… no pun intended."QCan you feel that, though? The stillness? I think we’re here for a reason."dLet’s look upstairs. You first, though – something’s off, and you’re the brave warrior."iNot that I want you putting yourself in harm’s way on my behalf… but it would be rather gallant."8Oh? I’ll refrain from reading too much into that.":What I’m worried about is something a bit less fun."TLet’s check upstairs, and be ready. You might end up having to save me again."Am I really that one-note?"]I’ll have to try and be more creative in the future – I can’t stand being cliché."QTo answer your question: I hope not, but there’s only one way to find out."8Shall we look upstairs? At your leisure, of course."fOh, no. I’m not going up there first. You’re the bold and brash one between us, aren’t you?"
