Fine."About time."I hate you too."I love you.000Iu;␀�[["{The fridge contains dozens of tupper-ware containers, all marked with dates as well as specific Pokemon species names.["S冰箱里有十几个保鲜盒，上面都标有日期和精灵的物种名。;["{The fridge contains dozens of tupper-ware containers, all marked with dates as well as specific Pokemon species names.Iu;␀;[[	"-A collection of Pokemon battling guides."<They seem like classics, likely more than 50 years old."A beat up old television."'It's been unplugged from the wall.[	" 精灵对战指南合集。"=相当经典得书，看起来得有50年的历史了。" 一台破旧的电视机。" 插头已经拔下来了。;[	"-A collection of Pokemon battling guides."<They seem like classics, likely more than 50 years old."A beat up old television."'It's been unplugged from the wall.0Iu;␀yi[[�"PLooks like the Trainer ahead is moving to block you from going any further."?Do you want to approach them? It looks like a tough fight."yI knew you would seek Yezera. I am her humble servant, naturally, though I would rather keep my identity enshrouded."JPray excuse the charade – it will not be necessary for much longer."jUnder Yezera’s profound guidance, we have achieved our goals. The titans have served their purpose."LI come then with a simple inquiry: will you not listen to my reasoning?"PThank you. Our goal is naught less than a complete reordering of the world."<My comrades have their own motives, but mine is simple."�The world at present is mercurial and deceptive. Human culture and technology serves as naught but a veil disguising ultimate truth."uOnly the realm of ancient myth, tended by gods, untouched by humans, might let us perceive it. Do you not agree?"tHow disappointing, to dismiss it outright. If you have no eye for truth, then we have nothing else to speak of."_Forgive me this act of passion, but I expect a titan’s wrath may settle my raging heart."Regice, heed my command."RTo the contrary: it has adamant support, if only one ruminates on the matter."`Such wavering faith is nigh-useless for my purposes, alas. We require unflinching devotion."_*sigh* I would be forsaking my duty if I did not stall you at the least. Prepare yourself."lI should encourage you to do so. Judge the weight of the world that is against the world that could be."bAlas, I know you will not ruminate idly upon it. You are a threat. That is intolerable to us."UThis shall be no decisive victory of mine, but I cannot let you pass unhindered."/…I should very much like to believe you."`If you speak truth, then I bid you repeat your convictions to Yezera herself next you meet."oShe can see the machinations of your heart more clearly than I. Until then, you remain a trainer, as do I."<My enemy I smite, my ally I train. To either, en garde."LIf you will not listen to my entreaties, then you are beyond salvation."VAlas. Perhaps a titan’s fury will enlighten you to the clarity of the ancients."TG’afternoon. Took your sweet time comin’ to find Yezera 'gain, didn’t ya?"CGot no interest in convincing you. Ain’t much of a preacher."�But I gotta set some ground rules 'fore we fight; establish some things. 'Cause we’re gonna fight. Ain’t no other way to it."SThank you kindly. I ain’t real interested in this cloak- and-dagger charade."I’m with Yezera, always."EListen, I’m only gonna say this once: you oughta hear her out.";Don’t care if you agree with her. Just hear her out."RAnd if you hurt her, I’ll make you wish Mavis stopped after Zain. We clear?"(Cocky li’l brat, ain’t ya? Tsk."uWhat’s so damn infuriating 'bout you is I ain’t just able to whip your sorry hide into submission. Too good."LHow 'bout I try anyhow? Titan’s gotta be good for somethin’, right?",Good. I ain’t 'bout ta repeat myself."BNow, I came here with a job to do, and I’m a reliable sort."[Sorry, kid. Yezera wants some peace 'n' quiet. Regice, lead us off, will ya darlin’?"VHah. Take it from someone who knows, kid: you ain’t even scratched the surface."AI can make you plenty more miserable if I set my mind to it."zBut, cheer up, kid. I’m 'bout to give ya what you always want: a good fight. Facing a Regi oughta cheer ya up. Heh."RNah, I ain’t about to trust that. Ya don’t know jack about me and Yezera."8Bickering old married couple, that’s what we are."9Want to show me you’re with us? Tell it to Yezera."rFor now, I ain’t too keen on letting you off easy. Sorry. Beating folks into the dirt is my job, after all."CAh, well. Guess no matter how hard I try, old habits die hard."BSpeaking of dying hard – lay down and quit moving, will ya?"PHah. They ain’t never been happy with my way of goin’ about covert ops."@Too rough 'nd tumble. I ain’t built for cloak-and-dagger."iSo, let me tell you straight: you listen to Yezera. You hear her out. And don’t you dare hurt her."KAll I ask. And, uh, I wasn’t just sent here to chit-chat. You ready?"Oh, hello."RSuch a picturesque place to meet. If only it were under better circumstances."]Regice and I have unfortunately been told to make sure Yezera has no unwelcome visitors."xBefore that, though… I know you’re more than a pretty face. You’ve got a spark to you. Will you listen to me?"0Aww. I knew I had a good feeling about you."[How do I explain it… well, I hate to use the word, but modern society is degenerate."_We’re distant from the perfect moment of creation. We’ve kind of taken over the world."UNo respect for our elders – the primordial Pokémon that created the universe."zYezera’s going to reset this world back to its origins. And then humanity will be in the bosom of Arceus once more."kDon’t call me insane. Although I’m sure this arrogant, faithless civilization would use that term."QI’m merely devout, and devotion means making sacrifices. For example: you."EI really do like you, but… we all have to sacrifice sometimes."MGodlike Pokémon are now treated as not much more than beasts of burden."MAvatars are destroyed at will because they’re “threats to humans.”"\The world has lost all respect, the divine essence from creation diluted and destroyed."NAnd since you seem to be no different, I can take some joy in this fight."�Arceus created the world. It is pure, and perfect, and resetting the world back to its original form will let us be pure and perfect too."BI’d like to see myself blessed by the grace of our creator.")I’d like to see you that way, too."In time."@For now, I’ve been ordered to remove you. Shall we dance?")Good. I knew I saw something in you."BSome spark of faith. I’m a… very good judge of character."�I’d love to just talk with you for a while, but I was explicitly instructed to stop you. So we’ll fight. Don’t take it personally."Oh. Was I too forward?"HMy emotions tend to get the better of me. I’m almost heartbroken."%Well, I suppose I am a stranger."�Fortunately, I’ve been sent to ensure you make it no farther, so I have a convenient vent for all these feelings of rejection.".Hello, friend. Yezera wishes to be alone."NTo that end, I have been sent, and graciously afforded a titan to aid me."`Before we attend to your removal, however, may I interest you in a short, frank discussion?"RI would rather like to try to convince you of the legitimacy of our position."Thank you for your time."_Yezera’s goal is to recreate the conditions of the world shortly following its creation."oModern science has attained almost complete understanding and mastery over the world – the modern world."�It cannot, however, understand the past. By reverting existence, we may study the universe from its conception and obtain universal knowledge."#This is the only way to do so."vWithout the reversion, humanity will never attain complete understanding of the universe. It is worth all prices."PNow our time for conversation is up, however. Regice, please do the honors."AAll persons who attempt to advance civilization should care."HUniversal knowledge is a prerequisite for an all- powerful society."\That is my goal. That is the goal of all science: to know, and to apply that knowledge."\Your ignorance implies discussion will get us nowhere. Let us dispense with such, then."<Knowledge will be retained into the new primordial era."8We can rebuild at least small enclaves of humanity."\From there our analysis and conquest will begin: a new society with absolute knowledge."@And, stemming from this absolute knowledge, absolute power."YConsider it. In the mean time, there is the business I mentioned earlier. Excuse me."|I am glad you have the wisdom to agree. If you should wish to support us in our endeavors, I will be happy to have you."xWe will fight for a more enlightened era. For now, however, I must slow you. Business is business. Let us commence."II find this highly unfortunate. You will be left behind by progress."NIf you would prefer to retain your ignorance, however, I cannot help you.",Prepare yourself. Regice, if you would."4Yo. Figure’d, uh, yeah, that you’d be here."bYezera’s here. You keep running into her. She, uh, doesn’t really want to talk right now."0I got a job to do, but, uh, not keen on it." So you want to hear us out?"]Swear we’ve got some good reasons. Even if I’m not that good at putting it in words."=Oh. That’s good. Great. Honestly didn’t expect that."HWell, I just figure we’ve done a lot of ordering Pokémon around.">Maybe it’s time to even up the footing a bit, y’know?"8We can all kinda make up for whatever we did wrong."mThe others have their reasons, but, uh, this is mine. Make a world where we can be forgiven. You get it?"(Well – fine. You know what? Fine."bI don’t need your permission, and we certainly don’t need your help. Regice. Do ‘em in."Z…You so sure? Takes a lot of pushing to train a team that strong in so little time."4But, yeah, no, I get it. Why would you help us?"?Rich brat. Maybe we can beat some responsibility into you."NUh. Don’t really know how to break it to you. You… don’t have time."EFor one, we’ve already just about won. For two – think fast!"(Regice, sweep ‘em off their feet!"*Oh. Didn’t, uh, really expect that.":Figured you were kind of a stuck-up brat. No offense."=Well, good. Maybe we’ll be side by side one day, yeah?"5But, uh, for now… I’m supposed to fight you."HSo, uh, sorry – ah, what am I saying, we live for this. Ready up."Yeah, I guess that tracks."#Fine. That’s… it’s fine."5I came here to beat the crap out of you anyways."iOdds are Regice isn’t gonna stick around much longer, so let’s make it count. Try your best, eh?"-Well. Had to happen eventually, I guess."II’ve kinda sorta been planning what to say for the past few hours."cBut, um… I still don’t know. So can I just say what comes to mind and hope you understand?"BWelp. Listen, uh, Makya’s kinda in a weird place right now."]Team Chasm ran roughshod over this whole region and then kinda just… got away with it?"So, uh, yeah, if you ever wanted proof that humans can’t get even the most black-and-white justice right, there you are."KWould’ve been simple to fix that little screw-up. But they didn’t."[So we’re taking the power away from humans, and putting it in the hands of Pokémon."Is it? Is it!"AAm I insane for wanting some damn PUNISHMENT in this world?!"DWell, guess what. If people won’t give me it, I’ll MAKE it.""And I’ve got just the tool!"%It is simple, you – you idiot!"aI can track down every ex-Chasm criminal and haul them up to the courts myself if I have to!"UThey just won’t do anything if I did! So I have to do things personally, yeah?" Sorry. Nothing… personal."	Yes!"MThey’re noble and pure and – and – and they’d never let me down!"/Unlike you! And everyone else around here!"JYou want to see? C’mon. See what kind of justice Pokémon can give!"Oh. Ah-hah."LKinda got myself a bit worked up there… welp, no harm, no foul, yeah?"…Nah, that’s stupid."^I’m not gonna waste this chance. I’ve got a Regi. You’re a prodigy. Let’s RUMBLE!"Urgh, you make me so mad!")Nobody will frickin’ listen to me!"
Fine."Y’know, fine, whatever."?You get what everyone else I fight gets. What you deserve."ARegice – your service has ended. If you would go, then go."YSo it returns to its resting place… no matter. It has done all I desired and more."%As for you, we shall meet again."YWhen and where, fate shall decide, though I think I know where we shall settle this."8Do not pursue me. Your audience with Yezera awaits.""Seems Regice’s 'bout spent."ODidn’t exactly expect them to be so squirrelly, but them’s the breaks.".Figure it’s headin’ back to its home."eOne last thing, since you seem ‘bout ready to see Yez again: you hurt her and I’ll find you."=And it won’t just be for some play fight with animals."sG’evening, kid. I’ll be seein’ you. Keep in mind how nice it feels to be havin’ all your bones intact."9Au revoir, Regice. Enjoy your entombment, I suppose."XAnd as for you, I’m breathless. Speechless. You’re even better than I imagined."OIf you’d like to stop your pointless struggling against us, tell Yezera."4We’d love to have you. Until we meet again…"2I surmise Regice will now return to its tomb."SThe titans are temperamental and ill-suited to existence outside their crypts."0It is of no matter. Our victory comes soon."JYezera may be displeased in my performance, but she is understanding."GIn the end, this will make no difference. Thank you for your time."See ya, Regice."Ah, who am I kidding."cIf either of us is gonna see it again, it’ll be you. Couldn’t really hold a candle to you."UHad to try anyways, just for Yezera. And I’m gonna have to do it again, right?"VGood practice, I guess. Well, think about it – everything, y’know? I’m out."U*sigh* So long, Regice. You never really were my type, anyways, so head on home."HAnd as for YOU, well, next time we talk it’ll be in a fair world!"MIf it isn’t, then, uh, I’ll have to buy us a li’l more time, 'kay?"FUntil then, I’ve got judgment to be a-judging. So long, "hero.""No."	Yes."I'll listen."Don't need it."No, I don’t."That's tenuous."I'll think about it."
