 Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."?I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance. Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."]Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you. You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."\Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region. You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."MNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this! But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"UEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you. Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."bMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon. They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."xNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up. I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"%...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"~Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog. You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"zThat’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt! You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it."9Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Phione. I guess that was it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time.[�"你准备好了吗？"J即便到现在都无法阻止你...当然我也不是没有料到。"_你接受了叶泽拉的邀请，即便这会把你带到这个地区最凄凉的深渊。"q你认为自身是英雄吗？还是对某些事情怀恨在心？或者只是想要面对一位前冠军？";请不要告诉我，我更愿意自身猜出答案。"e我恐怕必须告诉你，虽然叶泽拉邀请了你，但我并不会向你提供的款待。"?你们2个可以在一个原始真理的世界里会面。")现在，让我窥探你的内心。"S我不会让你再往前走一步，一个揭示骗局的世界正等着我。"8我不会允许你否认我得到启迪的权利。"G我们开始不可避免的战斗吧，我等得有些厌倦了。"M人类的心灵，至少对于我的敏锐来说，是微不足道的。"\即使不考虑我的占卜，一个训练师的灵魂也会在战斗中裸露出来。",向我展示你的激情吧，英雄。"8你认为我说话的方式是虚伪的标志吗？"e随你便吧，你可以把我的话视为乏味或者过度，我也不再需要与你交谈。"G用你最能听懂的语言吧？恰好，我也很擅长这个。">你迟到了，小家伙。让女士等待很没礼貌。";哈！我说的女士不是自身，而是叶泽拉。"\收起你这份笑意，她打扮得好的时候很好看，而且她是我的朋友。"#她应当被尊重，明白？"~现在，我有些坏消息告诉你：如果我能阻止的话，我不会让你和她最后起舞，到这里就结束了。"M很高兴你愿意听我讲话，但现在，我不会手下留情的。"8不过，因为你的礼貌，我不会打伤你。"h但你毕竟在阻挠叶泽拉，那就留下一些淤青吧。准备好了吗？放马过来吧。"/啊，你的脸真的很和我的胃口。"M我挺想把你带回去见父母的，但现在我得让你下地狱。"D哈哈！我开玩笑的，我不会再做得那么极端了。"G但是我也不会让你毫发无损地离开，准备好了吗？",你...听着，她...别让我分神。"P每次不得不带她去舞会时...她穿上礼服都比我好看多了。"V总之，要把她当做女孩子看待，像对待一位女士一样尊重她。"P啊，我不该分心想这些...别用心理战术了，跟我好好打。"A哈！随你怎么说，我只不过是做个比喻罢了。"Y你想接近她，就得先过我这关，虽然老套，但这就是我的底线。"8你也可以说，我是在准备序曲，哈哈！"M说实话我挺喜欢你的，但现在得把你的幽默打出来了。"n你好，你来得...比我预期中要早一些...我正在写一首诗，可惜永远无法完成了。"�这黑色的拱门像是没有星星的夜空，很快就要被华丽的雪花石膏所代替，可这却破坏了中心的象征意义。"A真可惜，我猜...你现在要逼我跟你决斗了吧？"D你闯进我的领地，带着你训练有素的战斗宠物。"h我们以前就交过手了，你还反对我的美好梦想，我又怎么有选择的权力呢？"_不要侮辱我了。你已经做出了选择，现在我们必须承担相应的后果。"\好吧，至少你很诚实，我喜欢你这一点，喜欢你如此清晰的思路。"�在这个阴暗的洞穴里，总有一束闪亮的光芒。这似乎也可以写成诗！如果我们能有一个陷入绝望的浪漫主义者来记录一切就好了。"J唉，我不得不将我的激情投入到分化你的团队当中。"k当然！你在这个地区是如此杰出的一束光，你应该得到颂歌...得到十四行诗。"}另一方面，你现在站在我对面而不是和我并肩作战，这意味着你并不像我想象中那么特别。"M没有信仰，真是可惜！我不想这样做！但我必须要做。";既然我这已经是定局...那就享受一下吧。"Y什么？你认为有诗意的灵魂很可怕吗？虔诚的信仰让你不安吗？"V不被无休止的社会劳作所侵扰的真实情感让你感到不舒服了？"Y好吧，享受那种狭隘的看法吧。也就是说：你将在这里输给我。"你好，朋友。"J我们已经开始行动了，雷吉奇卡斯将很快重塑世界。"S我知道你来这里是为了见叶泽拉的，但很抱歉我不能允许。"�你成功的概率接近于零，但我不是赌徒，不会选择放任。如果你愿意，我们可以一起待在这里，直到逆转影响到我们。"b我也是这么觉得的。不好意思，但在现在这种情况，我必须和你战斗。"k真正的知识正在接近，我想在那里见证它...如果可能的话，我也想独自一人。"b我也不想，不幸的是，我可以从你的语气中感觉到我们确实将要决斗。"Y我不愿让你继续前进，也不愿输给你。请理解...并考虑认输吧。"D如果你要直面叶泽拉，这已经是保守的估计了。"b只要她想，她就是无敌的，尽管我也听说了，你已经多次打破了惯例。"P现在，我们可以结束理论讨论，再引入另一部分数据吗？"J请原谅我啰嗦，如果你想直接进行决斗，那就来吧。"V我不会侮辱你的智慧，假装我们不会打架，那没有什么意义。"开始吧？"&哦...嗯...我直奔主题了。"G你曾经打败过我，也打败了叶泽拉，嗯...很多次。"k虽然其中一些场次，因为她用了别人的队伍，或者其他什么原因而不能算数。"_但问题是，我打不过你，也还是...必须尝试。我有很多问题要解决。"Y我必须去弥补自身曾经的过错，你就不能让我得到这个机会吗？"G没错，我知道是这个答案，你什么都不会让给我。"Y我本来那么努力，就要成为冠军的！但是...没错，一切都玩了！"S你很多方面都超过我了，我打不过你，但我会用其他方式！"w对你来说可能是这样，但对它们来说不是...不是对精灵来说，是那些必须原谅我的人。"n是时候让他们不再接受命令，被平等对待了。这也包括像你这样的顶尖训练师。"h我知道你不能容忍这一点，所以...我想我们得打一架，抱歉...但我不后悔。"&大多数时候我不会这样。"t我正在尽我最大的努力去改正曾经的错误，你敢说这样的话吗？你只是在维持现状。"k这是你想要的世界吗？你是个富家子弟，所以...没错，没有压力，生活美好。"M哼，如果可以的话，我会让你的生活变得更艰难一些。"2抱歉，或许我就是个恶毒的混蛋。"e不！我会失败的...我很乐意失败...但我不会放弃。我有需要保护的朋友。"D我有需要去弥补的过去，有需要去建设的世界。"{一个更好的世界...一个更加平等、公正的世界。对，这不是你想要的，但我不会因此而屈服。"准备好了吗？")...嘿。这在这里了，对吧？"S你不会...大概...改变主意对吗？忽略了正义、公平和惩罚？"h呵，是我看走眼了...你就是塔玛琳的走狗，大概...从一开始就在为她做事！"J你知道这意味着什么吗？没错：是时候付出代价了！"~没错，他们也这么说，你不是这个团队的普通士兵，你...大概...是个...暂时失去权势的策划者！"e呵，你们都一样，我已经干掉了很多士兵了，这次也不会有有什么例外！")不，我真的真的很想打你！"\既然我打不到塔玛琳，那你就是最好的选择，过来让我揍你一顿。";如果你真的抱歉，就别再继续了，白痴！"q你真是个...蠢货！我怎么才能让你明白你是坏人？我能把这些打进你的脑袋里吗？"q如果必须的话，我会卷起袖子亲自揍你！如果弄坏了我的指甲，我甚至会杀了你！"8来吧，我的队友们！我们要打败他们！"啊。哈，哈哈哈！"�就这样吧！预言已经完成了...这场战斗在这里留下的，这些古老石头上的伤痕，就是未来的预兆。"J你能猜到它说了什么吗？它说我会失败，你会获胜。",哈！命运似乎有一种幽默感。"S继续吧，去更深处。我知道我的位置，不会再违抗命运了。"V为了我的理智，我将不再尝试预测你未来战斗的结果。告辞。"哦，你不该这样。"_你对我全力以赴了？我觉得连一半都没有，你完全就是在享受战斗。"�继续吧，叶泽拉在等你，我对计划是否成功并不在意，无论结局如何，叶泽拉都会变成一个勇敢的女孩。"_一定...比我更坚强，所以你去做你计划中的事情吧，无论那是什么。"t还有如果你敢伤害她，尸体永远都不会被找到，吧啦吧啦吧啦，你知道我要说什么。",祝你好运吧，之后再来找我。";...走吧，现在就走吧。在我发火之前走。"D宇宙的命运真的取决于我们训练精灵的技能吗？"h这太荒谬了！太愚蠢了！我简直不敢相信...走！走！我应该...我应该...走！"z我知道了，请原谅我...我根本没有提供足够的力量，我发现自身没有任何挑战你的手段。"S...明白了，我别无选择，只能撤退，祝你接下来厄运缠身。"A如果你允许我离开，我不会再阻碍你的进展。"&再见...还是别再见的好。"该死！该死！"D我...对，就是这样。我从来不像你们那样厉害。"b我努力训练我的精灵，试图达到那个水平，现在...试图弥补所有过错。"M对不起，大家。对不起，玛纳霏。我想那就是结局了。"\让我们把你们送回精灵中心，好吗？让你们恢复过来...我很抱歉..."8呃！我...没事！哎，我想我挨了一枪..."t看着我的眼睛，你这个愚蠢的家伙！如果我不是...呃...如果我不是...我...有点头晕..."V这就是他们输掉之后...会晕倒的原因吗？我...我要...我不行..."A你这个榆木脑袋...去做...大概...你想做的吧..."h但你毕竟在阻挠叶泽拉，那就留下一些淤青吧。准备好了吗？放马过来吧。"Y你想接近她，就得先过我这关，虽然老套，但这就是我的底线。"M对不起，大家。对不起，霏欧纳。我想这就是结局了。"&我早就该想到她没用了。"b叶泽拉就差一点，就差一点，如果她没有告诉你，那就能得到一切了。"�她就不该是人类，她唯一的可取之处，就是她身上非人性的成分。现在她背叛了它，也背叛了我。"8外表上或许吧，但实际上有够恶心的。"b和其他人一样，只有肤浅、愚蠢的欲望，我想我和她一样都是个白痴。")对对对，很好。为她高兴。"e但这无论是对她的，还是我的计划都不是好事，希望这种宣泄是值得的。"D是的，她做到了，我很高兴你能意识到这一点。"/好吧，希望永远不会再见到你。"2但是，结束之后，我会照顾她的。">但你，我现在就得处理掉，就这样再见吧。"G想让我再处理你一次吗？来吧，想多少次都可以。"不！")我需要它！我非常需要它！"5我会...你不明白，你什么都不明白。",你们这些生物让我感到恶心。"5好吧，你赢了。去和叶泽拉会合吧。"2我希望她能让你明白自身的位置。";如果再见面，对我们谁来说都不会好过。"我要走了。"不。"是的。"你要阻止我？"让开"你觉得你能？"闭嘴吧"那好吧"我不想这样"打扮好的？"能否起舞由我决定"我没有强迫你"对，来吧"给我的诗？"还是很恶心"不可能"我不想打架"接近于零？"说够了吧"不行"这是错的"不要自怨自艾"放弃吧"我不是她的手下"必须这样做？"对不起"那就来吧"她是人类"她做得很好"她做到了" 闭嘴，是时候算账了;[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."?I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance. Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."]Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you. You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."\Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region. You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."MNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this! But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"UEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you. Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."bMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon. They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."xNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up. I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"%...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"~Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog. You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"zThat’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt! You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it."9Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Phione. I guess that was it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time.00Iu;␀�,[[]"	\PN."gY’know, I pretty much assumed this was going to be a trap, but I didn’t think you’d be here.",Well... whatcha doing? Care to explain?"7What? You want me to explain this? Velenz? *shrug*">Oh, I know. But you’re the one standing in front of me."LCute. Never should’ve brought a hero here. Heroes are always trouble.")*snort* Sure, kid. Whatever you say."vI know you’re here with that girl – Candy? Helena’s had her trackers keeping an eye on her for a while now."JShe hasn’t been causing too much trouble, though, so we let her go."dListen, we ran this region. Do you know what that means – taken any political science lately?"JIt means a monopoly on violence. Every government works the same way."BOh, you can call me a tyrant if you want, but I’m no thief."Yep! And a damn good one."fNot an absolute one, though – Andris and Helena made up the other two corners of that triangle."JNot to mention the extensive bureaucracy of Team Chasm at its height."@From who? This was a lawless frontier before we came along."VOnly holdouts like Novo truly resisted unification into the larger establishment."hThe benefits of being a tyrant. If people are getting in the way, you can convince them to... stop."/C’mon. You were raised better than that."8We still rule the region because we ARE the region."�We’ve got old grunts everywhere who’ll still follow orders if I give them. Helena has her trackers, so we’ve got an intelligence agency."dAnd she’s got her claws in LuxTech’s outpost here, so economic development is guided by us."XWe were a big organization. All-encompassing. And we had to be: lots of work to do."uOver just a few decades, we imposed law on this place, created entire new settlements, made it rich and vibrant."�We quintupled the population. We dealt with outbreaks, infighting, earthquakes. We secured the support of multiple major companies."~And at the end of the day, we managed to go legit, integrate with the Prizcan government, and aren’t even hated for it."_If you want to try and do even a tenth of that without resorting to violence, be my guest."�We punished people, which you’d call assault. We imprisoned them, which you’d call kidnapping. We taxed them, which you’d call theft."FOh, sure, people resisted us, but we only acted how a state does."ECandy’s too young to have been around during Chasm’s zenith."~She’s got a child’s notion of justice, and she thinks that performing her own little acts of violence fixes anything."GMaybe she should ask herself why almost everyone’s fine with us."	Yes."Andris did it for money."Helena did it for power."WAnd I did it so I could finally have the resources to properly research the Regis."ZEveryone in Team Chasm – in any organization – has their own reasons to be there."F...We can argue all day, kid. You’re not going to get anywhere."Let me put it this way:"�a lot of the Pokémon Candy has “rescued” were given to Chasm grunts for combat purposes, but they ended up liking their new home plenty fine."PMaybe talking things out would’ve resolved things better than theft, huh?"gBut I know you want to know. What’s up with Velenz? Well, it’s simple. We were trying to work."�I can’t work when I’m being attacked by wannabe heroes. When the power grid is being fried. When Ghost-types are being sent to haunt my lab.";We asked, repeatedly, for them to stop. They didn’t."tSo I took Regigigas and had it carve up the bedrock around here, then dragged some avatars in for good measure."zThey couldn’t prove it was us, but pretty soon they lost their base of operations, and that got the message across."LYes. Was. If they’d wanted to keep it, they could’ve left us alone."?Kid, have you ever gotten twelve hours of sleep in a week?"vThese “freedom fighters” were using every trick in the book. Constantly harrying us. Never a moment’s rest.".Ugh. Makes me mad just thinking about it."I think so, yeah."NThat’s how it goes. Warfare ain’t pretty, but it exists for a reason."qI did what I did. And if someone wants to “bring me to justice” for it, I say: what does that even mean?"LI’m breaking my back running this region, making it better every day."fYou want to throw me in prison? Make this place worse so you can have your petty revenge? Idiocy."SI know what I did, and I’m not going to do it again. Neither is anyone else."|...Now, kid. I need to get out of this place, because I don’t particularly want to run into Candy. Get out of my way."NYou need to work on your active listening. I didn’t ask you a question."MI told you what you were going to do… and now you’re going to do it."Ugh. Heroes!"3Damn heroes... well, what’d I really expect."Get up."CI’m not angry, just disappointed. But I will be taking my–"\PN! Tamarind!"xStop right there. I – I know I took, um, a little bit to get here, but that’s only because I was eavesdropping!";Candy, is it? Good to meet you in person... I suppose."5You know where I stand. And I know where you do."�I’ve just settled things with \PN, so why don’t we have a chat in private? \PN, be a dear for me and leave us. I’d like to end this grudge here and now."Z...Alright. This is between you and me, anyways. \PN, you can go, like, wait outside."+Just for a minute. This’ll be quick.".Good. Glad we can see eye to eye on this."You first."Not my idea."Getting answers."Delivering justice."Tyrant."You seized power."And Velenz?"You don't rule anymore."Not just violence."Some hate you."You did it for yourself."It was their home."That seems excessive."Fair enough."..."No."...Alright.[]"\PN。"J我一开始就觉得这是个陷阱，但没想到你会在这里。"/嗯...能解释一下你在做什么吗？"4什么？我解释这个？夜幽市？*耸肩*"G嗯，我能猜到，但现在你是站在我面前的那个人。"_笑话。永远不要把英雄主义带到现实中，英雄总是会给大家添麻烦。";*哼* 随便吧，孩子，你说什么就是什么。"e我知道你和那个...叫糖儿的女孩在这里。海伦娜已经注意她很长时间了。"M不过，她并未造成太多麻烦，所以我们也就没太在意。"k听着，我们统治着这个地区，你应该明白这意味着什么...你最学过政治学吗？"J政治就是需要一些暴力手段，每个政府都是一样的。"5你可以管我叫暴君，但我不是小偷。",而且还是一个非常出色的人。"]但也不是绝对的...安德里斯和海伦娜组成了这个地区的另外2个角。"P更别说裂隙队最鼎盛时期，那庞大且复杂的官僚系统了。"e从谁那里夺走的？在我们来这里之前，马凯亚更是一个无法无天的地区。"V除了最初望新镇的那群顽固分子，其他人都不抵触融入我们。"n成为暴君的好处是什么？如果有人故意与你做对，你可以“说服”他们停下来。",呵，本以为你的家教会更好。"J我们仍然统治着这个地区，因为我们就是这个地区。"�这里的每一处土地上都有我们的老兵，只要一声令下，他们便会服从。海伦娜也有她自身的追随者，因此我们有了庞大的情报网络。"n是她在光华市现在的位置创造了那座城市的一切，并依靠科技发展我们的经济。"e我们是一个庞大的组织，无所不包，无所不有，因为我们必须得这样做。"�我们用了仅仅几十年的时间，便在这里颁布了法律，创建了人类的聚落，使其变得富有且充满活力。"�这个过程中，马凯亚的人口增长了5倍，我们处理了疾病、自然灾害，还有一次又一次的内部纷争，并获得了多家大公司的支持。"~并最终得以与宏礼市的政府融合，在将混乱控制在最小的情况下，让一切平稳过渡到现在这样。"h如果你觉得想要达成这个目标，一点暴力都不需要使用，那就自身试试吧。"{我们对罪犯的惩罚被视为攻击，我们对他们的监禁被视为绑架，我们对他们征税被视为盗窃。"J当然，有不少人反对过，但是国家的发展更加重要。"J糖儿她毕竟年纪小，没有经历过裂隙队的鼎盛时期。"V她对正义的概念像个孩子，认为自身的小暴力可以解决问题。"\我觉得她应该问问自身，为什么几乎其他所有人都对我们很满意。"没错。" 安德里斯是为了钱。"#海莲娜是为了权力欲。"A我这么做是为了能有足够的经费来研究巨人。"_裂隙队里的每个人...不管在哪个组织中，他们都有自身的利益诉求。"\...孩子，就这个问题，我们可以争论一整天，但不会有任何进展。"这么说吧："{糖儿所“拯救”的那些精灵，的确是因战斗目的而征收的，但它们也渐渐喜欢上了新的生活。"q你觉得它们真的想回到原主人身边吗？就算是，那谈判也比偷窃更容易解决问题。"A我知道你最关心的，还是夜幽市的情况对吧？"�很简单，我们在正常工作的时候，被一些自称为英雄的人攻击了，他们烧毁了电网，并派出幽灵精灵去骚扰实验室。"P我们一次又一次地，要求他们停下来，但显然没什么用。"t所以我只能带着雷吉奇卡斯，去那里打通地下隧道，并创造出一些化身来保护设施。"}在我们反攻之后，他们很快就丢盔弃甲了，如今夜幽市的样子就是这一场骚乱的直接结果。"e是的，过去是的。不过如果他们想保住它，只要不来打扰我们就可以了。"4你有过一周只睡12个小时的经历吗？"�这些所谓的“自由战士”几乎把你能想到的诡计都用了一遍。在不断地骚扰下，我们很多人每天只能睡一2个小时。"啊...想想就来气。"我就说吧。"G事实就是，战争并不美好，但它存在是有原因的。"}我只是做了自身该做的事，如果有人想要因此“将我绳之以法”，那我只想说：那又怎样？"D我正在努力经营这个地区，让它每天变得更好。"q你要把我送进监牢吗？这只会让这个地方变得更糟，唯独满足了你小小的报复心。"k我很清楚以前做过些什么，但之后不会，也不需要再做了，当然其他人一样。"Y现在，孩子，我该离开这个地方了，因为我不想碰巧遇到糖儿。"J你需要改善你的思维方式，而且我并不是在询问你。"5我只是告诉你，你现在需要这样做。"呃...英雄？">去特么的英雄...好吧，我到底在期望什么？"起来。">我没有生气，只是失望。但我会带走我的..."\PN！塔玛琳！"Y站住！我...我知道我来晚了，但那只是因为想听听你们说什么！";糖儿是吗？很高兴亲自见到你...大概吧。"2你知道我的立场，我也知道你的。"�我刚刚解决了与\PN的谈话，所以为什么我们不私下聊聊呢？\PN，你先离开一下吧。我想在这里结束这场仇恨。"S...这是我们之间的事情，\PN，你可以走了，在外面等一下。"#只需要一分钟，很快...";很高兴我们在这个问题上能够达成一致。"你先说。"不是我的主意。"寻找答案。"追求正义。"暴君。"你夺取了权力。"那夜幽市呢？" 你不再统治这里了。"不仅仅是暴力。"有些人恨你。"你是为自身而做。"那是他们的家。"似乎有些过分。"有道理。"..."不。"...好吧。;[]"	\PN."gY’know, I pretty much assumed this was going to be a trap, but I didn’t think you’d be here.",Well... whatcha doing? Care to explain?"7What? You want me to explain this? Velenz? *shrug*">Oh, I know. But you’re the one standing in front of me."LCute. Never should’ve brought a hero here. Heroes are always trouble.")*snort* Sure, kid. Whatever you say."vI know you’re here with that girl – Candy? Helena’s had her trackers keeping an eye on her for a while now."JShe hasn’t been causing too much trouble, though, so we let her go."dListen, we ran this region. Do you know what that means – taken any political science lately?"JIt means a monopoly on violence. Every government works the same way."BOh, you can call me a tyrant if you want, but I’m no thief."Yep! And a damn good one."fNot an absolute one, though – Andris and Helena made up the other two corners of that triangle."JNot to mention the extensive bureaucracy of Team Chasm at its height."@From who? This was a lawless frontier before we came along."VOnly holdouts like Novo truly resisted unification into the larger establishment."hThe benefits of being a tyrant. If people are getting in the way, you can convince them to... stop."/C’mon. You were raised better than that."8We still rule the region because we ARE the region."�We’ve got old grunts everywhere who’ll still follow orders if I give them. Helena has her trackers, so we’ve got an intelligence agency."dAnd she’s got her claws in LuxTech’s outpost here, so economic development is guided by us."XWe were a big organization. All-encompassing. And we had to be: lots of work to do."uOver just a few decades, we imposed law on this place, created entire new settlements, made it rich and vibrant."�We quintupled the population. We dealt with outbreaks, infighting, earthquakes. We secured the support of multiple major companies."~And at the end of the day, we managed to go legit, integrate with the Prizcan government, and aren’t even hated for it."_If you want to try and do even a tenth of that without resorting to violence, be my guest."�We punished people, which you’d call assault. We imprisoned them, which you’d call kidnapping. We taxed them, which you’d call theft."FOh, sure, people resisted us, but we only acted how a state does."ECandy’s too young to have been around during Chasm’s zenith."~She’s got a child’s notion of justice, and she thinks that performing her own little acts of violence fixes anything."GMaybe she should ask herself why almost everyone’s fine with us."	Yes."Andris did it for money."Helena did it for power."WAnd I did it so I could finally have the resources to properly research the Regis."ZEveryone in Team Chasm – in any organization – has their own reasons to be there."F...We can argue all day, kid. You’re not going to get anywhere."Let me put it this way:"�a lot of the Pokémon Candy has “rescued” were given to Chasm grunts for combat purposes, but they ended up liking their new home plenty fine."PMaybe talking things out would’ve resolved things better than theft, huh?"gBut I know you want to know. What’s up with Velenz? Well, it’s simple. We were trying to work."�I can’t work when I’m being attacked by wannabe heroes. When the power grid is being fried. When Ghost-types are being sent to haunt my lab.";We asked, repeatedly, for them to stop. They didn’t."tSo I took Regigigas and had it carve up the bedrock around here, then dragged some avatars in for good measure."zThey couldn’t prove it was us, but pretty soon they lost their base of operations, and that got the message across."LYes. Was. If they’d wanted to keep it, they could’ve left us alone."?Kid, have you ever gotten twelve hours of sleep in a week?"vThese “freedom fighters” were using every trick in the book. Constantly harrying us. Never a moment’s rest.".Ugh. Makes me mad just thinking about it."I think so, yeah."NThat’s how it goes. Warfare ain’t pretty, but it exists for a reason."qI did what I did. And if someone wants to “bring me to justice” for it, I say: what does that even mean?"LI’m breaking my back running this region, making it better every day."fYou want to throw me in prison? Make this place worse so you can have your petty revenge? Idiocy."SI know what I did, and I’m not going to do it again. Neither is anyone else."|...Now, kid. I need to get out of this place, because I don’t particularly want to run into Candy. Get out of my way."NYou need to work on your active listening. I didn’t ask you a question."MI told you what you were going to do… and now you’re going to do it."Ugh. Heroes!"3Damn heroes... well, what’d I really expect."Get up."CI’m not angry, just disappointed. But I will be taking my–"\PN! Tamarind!"xStop right there. I – I know I took, um, a little bit to get here, but that’s only because I was eavesdropping!";Candy, is it? Good to meet you in person... I suppose."5You know where I stand. And I know where you do."�I’ve just settled things with \PN, so why don’t we have a chat in private? \PN, be a dear for me and leave us. I’d like to end this grudge here and now."Z...Alright. This is between you and me, anyways. \PN, you can go, like, wait outside."+Just for a minute. This’ll be quick.".Good. Glad we can see eye to eye on this."You first."Not my idea."Getting answers."Delivering justice."Tyrant."You seized power."And Velenz?"You don't rule anymore."Not just violence."Some hate you."You did it for yourself."It was their home."That seems excessive."Fair enough."..."No."...Alright.0Iu;␀�[["(Its full of bait to use in fishing."6You an angler? Nah, you don't much look the type."&More like the type to own a boat!"AFor a fee I can let ya park your boat on the dock out front."?Alright, just sign here... and, it's legally yours to use."0Hope your trips on the Eleig are enjoyable!">You don't have the cash? My read on you musta been wrong."Alright, fair's fair."!That your boat? Whoooeeeeeh."It's a real beauty." Got any good fishing spots?"9Myself, I got a secret spot up on the Highland Lake."7Or maybe I should say "down" in the Highland Lake."!...maybe I've said too much.[",里面装满了用于钓鱼的饵料。"A你是个钓鱼佬吗？不，你看起来不像那种人。"#更像是那种有船一族！">只要你肯付费，就可以在这里租一个船位。"M谢谢惠顾，在这里签字...现在，这个船位就是你的了。"5希望你能喜欢在埃利格的航行时光！")你没钱？难道我看走眼了？"好的，谢谢惠顾。"#那是你的船吗？哇哦。"这艘船真不错。"#有什么好的钓鱼点吗？",我在云上湖有一个秘密钓点。"2准确的说，是云上湖的“下面”。" ...我说这么多干嘛...;["(Its full of bait to use in fishing."6You an angler? Nah, you don't much look the type."&More like the type to own a boat!"AFor a fee I can let ya park your boat on the dock out front."?Alright, just sign here... and, it's legally yours to use."0Hope your trips on the Eleig are enjoyable!">You don't have the cash? My read on you musta been wrong."Alright, fair's fair."!That your boat? Whoooeeeeeh."It's a real beauty." Got any good fishing spots?"9Myself, I got a secret spot up on the Highland Lake."7Or maybe I should say "down" in the Highland Lake."!...maybe I've said too much.Iu;␀U[[B"%It's hard for me to fit in here."PI was only invited as a reward for most lines of code written last quarter."@Is that even such a good metric of productivity? I dunno...",Welcome to the party! Want a moon rock?"zNo, seriously. I was on the space shuttle launch in Alola last month - we brought all kinds of Pokémon back with us!"mThese ones didn't wind up being useful for research, so I've just been handing them out as party favors."6I've got Solrock and Lunatone. Which do you want?"LYou sure? These rocks're pretty far from home. Could use a good friend."$We could all use a good friend."@Well, let me know if you change your mind. Enjoy the party!"DHere you are! One Solrock, fresh from the far reaches of space."AHere you are! One Lunatone, straight from the lunar surface."BGood memories on that mission, you know. Lots of new friends."0Like Lainie. I wonder what she's up to now?"What? Where am I?"What- oh... oh god..."6Space was so dark... so cold, and so very dark...")I need to go. I need to see the sun."EIsn't it a bit peculiar that this house is entirely symmetrical?"8And the mix of Kalosian and Kantonian aesthetics...";Maybe you'd disagree, but it rings a mite tacky to me."JThe most important thing to learn in your life is how to be generous."JI once gave $1,000,000 towards that Pokemon sanctuary west of Velenz."HJust talking about it has got me in a giving mood. Here, take this."KNow now, you wouldn't be asking me to give you another one, would you?"ZThe most important thing to learn in your life is how to be happy with what you have."Welcome, \PN!"*Oh, I can see the shock on your face."9I recognize you from pictures your mother showed me."PWe meet often at LuxTech events. She's a real business leader, your mother!"LI think it's fair for me to say that she's an inspiration to all of us."4I hope you enjoy yourself at our little soiree."NTrainers should just learn to surf with their Pokemon, like they used to."/My Feraligatr and I were quite the pair..."LNasty business, that thing with the bridge. Good thing I have a boat..."SThis piece was sculpted by Noel, the Gym Leader on the eastern half of Prizca."&I can tell just by looking at it!"[You know, I had a keen interest in Noel even before all that nonsense with Team Chasm."*I've really hit my stride at LuxTech."IMoving smart and talking fast. Striking deals and meeting deadlines."0I could never show off my talents in Chasm."AThe nerve they had to assign me to the docks, of all places."LHere you are, a specialty of the Kalos Region, made fresh this morning!">My deepest apologies, it seems we've run out of Galettes."2What in the world is wrong with this thing..."[You see the scientist struggle with a computer that is rapidly blinking and turns off."WThere's something up with this computer. If only I had a Porygon to work it out..."6Actually hey, could you go and get me one please?"�I've been needing one anyways, since I work with computers. So please do a trade with me for it, I'll figure out what to get you for it."iWell no rush, maybe it'll mysteriously start working again... and yes, I turned it off and on again.">Ah, alright. Check again with me if you change your mind."$Thank you, let's get it traded."nYou trade over the Porygon. It enters the computer, and a buzzing sound is heard as a Shedinja flies out."?You catch it to prevent it from causing any other trouble."{What the- it was actually a bug in there? Well damn, okay. You can keep it I guess, the computer is working perfectly."Thank you for this!"Maybe later."I'll take a Solrock."I'll take a Lunatone."No"Yes[B"我很难融入这里。"G我只是因为上季度写的代码行数最多才被邀请的。"2按行算真的合理吗？我不好评价..."2欢迎参加派对！要不要来个月岩？"q说真的。我上个月参加了阿罗拉的航天飞机发射——我们带回了各种各样的精灵！"S这些最终对研究没什么用，所以我干脆当派对礼物送人了。"2我有太阳岩和月石。你想要哪个？"J你确定？这些岩石离家可不近。它们需要个好朋友。"&我们大家都需要好朋友。"A要是你改变主意了就告诉我。派对玩得开心！">给你！一块太阳岩，刚从遥远的太空运来。"8给你！一块月石，直接来自月球表面。"D那次任务有不少美好回忆，认识了很多新朋友。"8比如莱妮。我想知道她现在在忙什么？"什么？我在哪儿？" 什么——哦...哦天..."D太空漆黑一片...寒冷刺骨，而且非常非常黑暗...",我得走了。我需要看看太阳。"G这所房子是完全对称的，你有没有感觉到很奇怪？"2虽说融合了卡洛斯和关都的美学..."A或许你不同意我的想法，但我的确觉得很俗。";人生最重要的，就是要学会对他人慷慨。"P我曾经向夜幽市西边的那个精灵保护区捐了1,000,000金钱。"S每次谈起这件事，都会让我感到由衷的满足。这个给你了。"D你不会希望我再给你一个吧？慷慨不是冤大头。"D人生最重要的，就是学会享受自身拥有的一切。"欢迎你，\PN！"&很惊讶我认识你，对吧。")你母亲给我看过你的照片。"_我们经常在光华市的集会上见面，她真的是一位榜样般的商业传奇！"2我相信这里很多人都是这么想的。"5我希望你在这个小聚会上玩得开心。"V训练师们应该学会跟他们的精灵们一起冲浪，就像以前那样。";我的大力鳄和我曾经是相当出色的组合...">过不了桥可太难受了，还好我自身有艘船..."G这个作品是东宏礼市的馆主，诺埃尔先生雕刻的。"我一看就知道！"M要知道我在裂隙队时期之前，就一直在关注诺埃尔了。"/我在光华市找到了自身的节奏。"G敏锐地行动，高效地交流，打成目标，满足期望。"G之前在裂隙队，我并没能很好地施展自身的才华。"G那时候他们居然把我分配到码头，真是离谱至极！"J这是今天早上新鲜制作的，卡洛斯地区的特色美食。";啊，非常抱歉，我们的煎饼已经卖完了。")这东西到底出了什么问题..."J你看到科学家正与一台快速闪烁并关闭的电脑搏斗。"A这台电脑有点问题。要是我有多边兽就好了..."&嘿，你能给我拿一个吗？"�反正我也需要一只，因为我经常和电脑打交道。所以请和我交换吧，我会想想给你什么作为回报。"S不急，也许它会神秘地重新启动...是的，我已经重启过了。">啊，好吧。如果你改变主意了，再来找我。"&谢谢，我们开始交换吧。"n你交换了多边兽。它进入电脑，随后一阵嗡嗡声响起，一只脱壳忍者飞了出来。"/你抓住了它，阻止它再惹麻烦。"t什么——里面真的有只虫子？好吧，该死。你可以留着它，电脑现在运行得很完美。"谢谢你！"也许下次吧。"我要一块太阳岩。"我要一块月石。"不"是;[B"%It's h