ROFL."?The insurance business is all about predicting the future."*Too bad I'm completely unpredictable!",Well, I definitely didn't predict that."<Excuse me, I've got to update my mathematical models..."GNo matter. Even a loss is just more data to feed to the algorithm.".Crunching numbers like Sharpedo, oh yeah."%I'm just here for business, kid."#Doing a run for a few friends."_I'm wondering what made those strange grassy holes in the Amber Hills and the Floral Maze."0There's another one out by the Fin as well."QI ain't one of those superstitious types, but they don't look natural to me."&This place's got some sick stuff.";Sometimes, the hacker lady gives me rips of old games.".The publisher isn't gonna like that, heh."No"YesIu;␀�[[9"8Leather- and cloth-bound books are neatly lined up."CYou can't imagine how much it would cost if they were damaged."KAn old, beaten up laptop. A couple dozen windows are open all at once."RSomething is being researched, but it's impossible to tell what specifically."QIt's Nora's laptop. She must have forgotten it in her hurry to get to Svait."XA map displayed on the screen shows a path to the west of the Ranger Station there."q“Over 2500 years ago, there existed a sect of itinerant priests who worshipped a Legendary Carver of Clay."^And by its hand, people were able to claim dominion over inhospitable lands high and low."sYet, despite their efforts, humanity was cast out from the lands where the primal forces of this world worked."gBack to the caves; which their species used to call home. Now the caverns would be their tombs…""sGuess I forgot to keep the door locked… but I can’t really turn away the esteemed Champion \PN, now can I?"sI don’t know why you’re here but, if I had to make a guess… you’re searching for something; like I am."GName’s Nora. I like to think of myself as a seeker of knowledge."mI took up a job as a janitor here to gain access to this library, since it’s sealed off to the public."?It’s not trespassing if they’re paying you to be here."jTeam Chasm apparently had roots in anthropology, based on all the records they’ve shoved away here."_Translated passages with way too many sticky notes go over all kinds of myths and legends."\One that caught my eye involves the Seekers, those ancient priests I mentioned earlier."tThey were ultimately destroyed by a great darkness that some protector deity was apparently equipped to handle."dBut, based on the fact that the Seekers disappeared, the guardian must have failed in its duty."Why? I don’t know."ZThe notes here make reference to materials that I can’t find anywhere in this room."?I’m thinking that these records have to exist elsewhere."�And I’m going to assume that they must have been saved digitally, as there’s nowhere else in the region with this much literature."mDo you think you can search LuxTech for any servers hosting data from before Team Chasm was established?"VI’ll keep on searching here in the meantime for something hidden in the stacks."7Let me know if you find something over at LuxTech."PI’ve only been finding fun facts, the kind you’d see on a moving truck."IDid you know that hexagons were an important symbols of the Seekers?";That’s apparently what inspired Team Chasm’s logo."You’re back! Excellent.":I managed to make a breakthrough while you were away."9Would you mind showing me what you’ve found first?"%You hand over the Old USB Drive.")Nora loads the device on her laptop."Fascinating."�This one file, Project Chrysopoeia Albedo, goes into great detail of a large volcanic eruption thousands of years ago which heavily impacted the region."uIt makes sense that the large clouds of ash would be devastating to a civilization in its technological infancy."BThis must be the "great darkness" that the Seekers mentioned."qPerhaps that’s also why they built what would become the underground ruins; like those found in Mt. Kilna?"CMaybe those places were meant to be safe spaces from the smog?"KWait, no. Why would they have built shelters if they had the guardian?"2Hahaha. This is the rush I’ve been seeking."0Questions whose answers are more questions."tAs for my own findings: I found references to an aboveground ruins site which might lead to what we’re after."GI’ll be waiting for you in <imp>Svait, on the upper level</imp>."6A beautifully illuminated religious-looking text."7The script looks familiar, but not enough to read."A regal figure.";According to the plaque, it's the First King of Makya."BAh, please don't touch those. I'm sending them in for repair."1You'd be surprised how brittle these can be.[9"2皮革和布面装订的书整齐排列着。"8你无法想象如果它们受损要花多少钱。"M一台破旧的笔记本电脑，同时有几十个窗口被打开了。"D有些还在研究中的内容，但看不懂具体是什么。"Y这是诺拉的笔记本电脑，她肯定是急着去霜皑镇，忘了带上它。"M屏幕上显示的地图上，有一条从霜皑镇往西走的小路。"`“2500年前，有一个巡回祭祀教派，一直崇拜着传说中的粘土雕刻师。"Y在它的帮助下，人们才得以在高低崎岖的荒凉土地上繁衍生息。"q尽管他们付出了许多努力，但人类终究还是被世界上最为原始的力量赶出了那里。"T洞穴，那是它们曾经的家园，洞穴，那将成为它们的坟墓...""_哦？看来我忘了锁门了...不过我也不能拒绝尊贵的冠军，\PN，对吧？"k我不知道你为什么来这里，但根据我的猜测...你应该像我一样，在找什么吧？"M我是诺拉，我一般喜欢将自身称为“知识的探求者”。"n为了能进入这座图书馆，我特意应聘了这里的管理员，毕竟这儿并不对外开放。"M现在我有正经理由待在这里，就不能算是非法入侵了。"h从他们藏在这里的记录来看，裂隙队显然也是从人类学开始一点点入手的。"h这些经过翻译的文献上，大大小小的全是便签，其中涉及到各种神话传说。"V我最在意的还是那些探索者...当然也可以管他们叫古代祭司。"}他们最终被庞大的黑暗能量毁灭，而他们所信仰的守护神，显然没有应对这种黑暗的方法。"Y那些探索者就此销声匿迹，而这位失职的守护神也不见了踪影。",至于具体的原因，我不知道。"J这里的注释当中提到了这个图书馆没有收录的材料。"5或许这些记录存在于其他什么地方。"z考虑到裂隙队，这些文献有可能是以数字形式保存下来的，不然我想不到它还会在哪儿。"z你能在光华市的档案中，搜索到一些裂隙队解散之前，所存放的数据或者服务器地址吗？"P当然，我也会试着在这里，找找有没有其他相关的内容。"G如果你在光华市找到些什么的话，就来告诉我吧。"P我这里只看到一些趣闻，类似在搬家卡车上那种小故事。";据说那些探索者的标志，是一种六边形。"/恐怕这也是裂隙队标志的来源。" 你回来了！太好了！"D在你去那边搜集材料时，我这里也取得了突破。"/能先给我看看你找到了什么吗？"你将旧U盘交给她。",诺拉将其链接在笔记本上了。"太惊人了。"�这份名为“莹润金成计划”的文件里，详细描述了数千年前的一次规模浩大的火山爆发，以及其对该地区造成的严重影响。"_大量的火山灰对于正处于技术萌芽阶段的文明造成了毁灭性的打击。",这一定就是“庞大的黑暗”。"\或许这就是他们建造地下城市的原因？就像基尔纳山发现的那些。"G或许这些地方本就是躲避火山灰影响的安全地带？";等等，不对劲！他们不是还有守护者吗？",哈哈哈，这就是我所追寻的！">问题接着答案，答案又会催生出新的问题。"}对了，还有我这边的发现：我找到一个地面废墟的参考资料，那里或许有我们要找的东西。"P我会到 <imp>霜皑镇上层</imp>，海拔稍微高点的地方等你。"/一本精美手绘的宗教风格文本。"5文字看起来熟悉，但还不足以读懂。" 一尊威严的人物像。"8根据牌匾，这是马凯亚的第一任国王。";啊，请不要碰那些。我要送它们去修理。",你会惊讶这些东西有多脆弱。;[9"8Leather- and cloth-bound books are neatly lined up."CYou can't imagine how much it would cost if they were damaged."KAn old, beaten up laptop. A couple dozen windows are open all at once."RSomething is being researched, but it's impossible to tell what specifically."QIt's Nora's laptop. She must have forgotten it in her hurry to get to Svait."XA map displayed on the screen shows a path to the west of the Ranger Station there."q“Over 2500 years ago, there existed a sect of itinerant priests who worshipped a Legendary Carver of Clay."^And by its hand, people were able to claim dominion over inhospitable lands high and low."sYet, despite their efforts, humanity was cast out from the lands where the primal forces of this world worked."gBack to the caves; which their species used to call home. Now the caverns would be their tombs…""sGuess I forgot to keep the door locked… but I can’t really turn away the esteemed Champion \PN, now can I?"sI don’t know why you’re here but, if I had to make a guess… you’re searching for something; like I am."GName’s Nora. I like to think of myself as a seeker of knowledge."mI took up a job as a janitor here to gain access to this library, since it’s sealed off to the public."?It’s not trespassing if they’re paying you to be here."jTeam Chasm apparently had roots in anthropology, based on all the records they’ve shoved away here."_Translated passages with way too many sticky notes go over all kinds of myths and legends."\One that caught my eye involves the Seekers, those ancient priests I mentioned earlier."tThey were ultimately destroyed by a great darkness that some protector deity was apparently equipped to handle."dBut, based on the fact that the Seekers disappeared, the guardian must have failed in its duty."Why? I don’t know."ZThe notes here make reference to materials that I can’t find anywhere in this room."?I’m thinking that these records have to exist elsewhere."�And I’m going to assume that they must have been saved digitally, as there’s nowhere else in the region with this much lit