 its arsenal."oSure, they managed to capture Heatran, the Titans, and other oddities I still need to comb that USB about."cBut were they so dominated by Yezera that they thought Volcanion wouldn’t make a difference?"eIt makes me realize how terrifying going against a single person with overwhelming power can be."...as you showed me, \PN."Anyway, ready?">Nora brings out a small MP3 player, and presses a button."<A soothing recording of an ancient flute fills the air."IAh. Seems like we have unwanted guests at this once private concert."6Awesome. At least they look in the mood to dance."SI guess we can crack some heads open, show them a genuine mosh pit experience."What do you think, \PN?"qAh. I realize now that, while I patched your team up after our battle, I’m out of supplies to heal my own."I’ll be counting on you!"What a painful cry…"�I can’t imagine how it must feel to wake up thousands of years after the disappearance of the people you were meant to protect."QI realize now that I’ve only thought about how others would USE Volcanion."6As a tool, a reward, or something in that vein…";I haven't been seeing this creature as a living being."!I saw it as words on a page."7Volcanion seems to be looking to you for guidance."Take Volcanion with you?"ENora, seeing your intent, comes over and hands you a Poké Ball."AThe Volcanion seems to sigh in relief as it enters the ball."Wonderful.">Well, I guess this is where we go our separate ways, \PN."JI hope you don’t mind, but I’m going to keep the USB you gave me."{Turning away from it all now would be to live a life knowing what passion is, but never permitting myself to experience it."{There are other loose ends left behind by Team Chasm, the Seekers, and who knows what else that I want to see through."Toodles."*Volcanion nods. It will wait for you."II still think it’d be for the best if you took Volcanion with you."DI’ve spent so much time looking towards the past for answers."BThough, I guess I can keep them com