inflict damage. Can random critical hit."iThe user blows up to inflict damage on all Pokémon in battle. The user faints upon using this move."MThe user's edges become sharper, raising its Attack stat by three steps."SThe user shoots a mysterious beam that changes the target's Ability to Simple."jIt enables the user to permanently learn the move last used by the foe. Once used, Sketch disappears."BBy slacking off, the user heals itself by half of its max HP."UThe target is attacked with a slash of claws or blades. Can random critical hit."eThis attack inflicts double damage on a numbed foe. It also cures the target's numbing, however."MThe user emits a snoring sound. This move can only be used while asleep."nThe power stored using the move Stockpile is released all at once in an attack. 150 base power per stack."`The user shines a spotlight on the target so that only it will be attacked during the turn."]The user stockpiles power, reducing move damage taken by 30%. This can be stacked twice."=Used only if the user has no PP. It also hurts the user."TThe user eats its held Berry, then raises Defense and Sp. Def by one step each."rThe user spends 25% HP to create a doll to protect it from move damage, additional effects, and status moves."dThe user chomps hard on the target with its sharp front fangs. It cuts the target's HP to half."PThe user generates odd sound waves from its body. The target becomes dizzy."fThe user consumes its Stockpile to heal itself by 50% of its max HP per stack. This can overheal."OStar-shaped rays are shot at the target. Can't miss and skips protections."SA physical attack in which the user slams into the target with its whole body."RA full-body attack for slamming into the foe. The user also takes 25% recoil."^The user gets teary eyed. This lowers the target's Attack and Sp. Atk stats by two steps."aThe user has teatime with all the Pokémon in the battle. Each Pokémon eats its held Berry."jThe user fires a beam of light at its target. The type changes depending on the Drive the user holds."JThe user performs a wobbly dance that dizzies the Pokémon around it."1The user rampages and attacks for two turns."]The user tickles the target into laughing, reducing its Attack and Defense by two steps."ZThe user transforms into a copy of the target right down to having the same move set."rThe user strikes with a simultaneous three-beam attack. It has a 15% chance each to numb, burn, or frostbite."eThe user unleashes its ultimate move. Can't miss and skips protections. Only one use per battle."mThe user attacks in an uproar, going on a rampage for two turns. Over that time, no one can fall asleep."]One turn after this move is used, the target's HP is restored by half the user's max HP."EThe user is roused, raising its Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps."[The user yawns, making the target drowsy. They'll fall asleep at end of the next turn."ZThe user looses a flurry of open-palmed arm thrusts that multi-hit two to five times."aThe user looses a blast of aura from deep within its body. Can't miss and skips protections."WThe user slams into the opponent, dealing damage based on the user's Defense stat."aThe user attacks with a swift chop. It also breaks any screens protecting the target's side."YThe user tenses its muscles to bulk up, raising its Attack and Defense by two steps."wThe user fights the foe up close without guarding itself. This lowers the user's Defense and Sp. Def by two steps."WThe user coaches its ally Pokémon, raising their Attack and Defense by two steps."^A retaliation move that counters any physical attack, inflicting double the damage taken."QThe user delivers a chop with its forearms crossed. Can random critical hit."FThe target is quickly kicked twice in succession using both feet."TAn energy-draining punch. The user's HP is restored by 33% of the damage dealt."aThe user punches the target with full, concentrated power. It dizzies the target if it hits."[The user risks all to attack the foe. The 