s a 40% chance to cause a flinch."@The user applies anesthetic substances, numbing the target."sThe user uses wind to blast its leaves at the target. This lowers the user's Defense and Sp. Def by two steps."uThe user gracefully slashes the target three times. The next time this move is used, it will hit one extra time."dFlowers blooms with intensity, damaging the target and raising the user's Sp. Atk by two steps."TRestores a fainted Grass-type party member to full HP. Only one use per battle."qThe user fades into the foliage, charging and becoming hidden, then strikes from stealth on the second turn."pThe user drops some heads from high up. The taller the user compared to the target, the greater the damage."nThe user flicks its thorns, dealing damage and setting a hazard layer of poison spikes around the target."eThe user fires a bolt of life energy at the target. It has a 20% chance to raise user's Sp. Atk."RThe target is disoriented by an explosive seed. It has a 30% chance to dizzy."KRound objects are hurled at the target to strike three times in a row."cThe user attacks the target with the power of a warding charm. Super effective vs Ghost-types."�The user keeps time for the team while attacking. Raises user's and allies' Speed and Accuracy. Counts as a Sound and Kick move."sThe user sheathes its blade. If hit by a foe's special move, it unsheathes it quickly, slashing all near foes."^The user uses their feet to pierce the foe. This has a 10% chance of leeching the target."RThe user eats decaying leaves, restoring its HP by 50% and raising its Speed."fThe target eats a strange seed. They become numbed if faster than the user, or leeched if slower."YCreates an odd flower to throw and damage a foe. Odd Room is created for five turns."PThe user stirs up a violent petal tempest and attacks everything around it."@The target is irritated by allergenic plants, poisoning it."hThe user bursts a ball of sleep-inducing powder. It fails unless the target hit the user this turn."NAttacks while destroying rooms. This move fails in the absence of a room."]The user kicks into the target like roots into earth. This has a 30% chance of leeching."]Halves attack damage taken this turn. Leeches any attackers. Fails if used successively."gLays roots that heal the user by absorbing 1/8th HP from foes each turn. The user becomes trapped."zSaps an enemy lured into its jaws. If they hit the user this turn, the user's HP is restored by 66% the damage dealt."[Attacks with energy from jealousy. All opposing Pokémon with stat boosts get leeched."QA parasitic seed leeches the target and reduces both its Attack and Sp. Atk."OThe user and the target each share their highest stat step with the other."OAttacks by gliding on the ground. This move always goes first in sunshine."gThe user calms itself and its teammates, raise its Sp. Def by three steps, and its allies' by one."VA nutrient-draining attack. The user's HP is restored by 75% of the damage dealt."aThe user makes a scary sound by shaking, forcing the target to switch out. Always goes last."UThe user wraps the target in its vines, trapping and binding it for three turns."_The user whips their legs into the target like a plant. This has a 10% chance of leeching."|Guaranteed to critical hit if the target has no stat step changes. The target is surged forward, raising all its stats."nThe user assists an ally's next move, boosting its power by 50% and letting it move right after the user."QA flare of electricity creates a bright light, damaging all nearby battlers."@The user charges, can used instantly for half of its power."TFor the rest of the round, the target's healing is reversed. Always goes first."�The user and the target pit their energy against one another. The damage is based on the target's Sp. Atk rather than their Sp. Def."�The user surges with electricity. If it deals less than 50% of the target's max health, the user takes the difference as recoil."jThe user wraps their body in electricity and crashes into the target. The user also takes 20% recoil."FRestores a fainted party member to 1 HP. Only one use per battle."cThe user breaks down all insulation to send a barrage of electricity to rampage for two turns."_The user harnesses a blade of lightning and slices at the target. Can random critical hit."PThe user lets out an electric roar, raising the user's Speed by four steps."xThe user attacks with courage. Sets a Spikes hazard layer if Full. If Hangry, deals double damage and is Dark-type."rThe user dances to heal an ally by half of their max HP. They're cured of any non-volatile status conditions."jCloaking itself in light energy, the user shocks the target, raising the user's Sp. Def by two steps."SDeals 50% more damage if faster than the target. This lowers the user's Speed."pThe target is pranked by an electric jolt. They are taunted and unable to use status moves for three turns."[The user strikes the enemy while coated with electricity. It has a 10% chance to numb."jElectricity is generated to beam intense light directly at the target. This has a 30% chance to numb."dThe user dances with the speed of lightning, raising its Sp. Atk by two steps and Speed by one."WThe user slams down into the target with electricity. It has a 10% chance to numb."rThe user lays a hazard around the foe. It deals Electric-typed 1/12th HP damage, or double that in rainstorm."ZThe user dances to encourage its ally. Their attacks this turn will be critical hits."�The user coils its body to generate an electric field, levitating for five turns and raising its Attack and Sp. Def by two steps."[The user finds the highest base power move among your able party members, and uses it."9A weak electric jolt is launched to numb the target."~The user slices with claws of light that have a 50% chance to numb. Can random critical hit. Counts as a Light and Slice move."rSends a pulse to flip the polarity of those nearby to damage a foe. Polarized Room is created for five turns."ePuts the target into a quarantine, trapping and disabling the move it last used for three turns."SThe target is struck with an electric current and multi-hit two to five times."|This move creates a directional magnetic field which reduces damage from attacks with 100 or more base power for five turns."VTurns the foe's power against it, dealing damage using the target's Sp. Atk stat."aAn electrified cloud zaps the target, lowering their Speed. This has a 50% chance to flinch."WThe user charges, then attacks on the second turn. Charges instantly in rainstorm."NThe user erupts with powerful yellow light to damage and numb the target."WThe user creates an electric fueled cage, trapping and binding it for three turns."jThe user takes an entire grid of power into its belly to slam the target. The user takes 100% recoil."~The user chomps down with high-voltage fangs. It has a 20% chance to numb and a 20% chance to lower Defense by two steps."jLaunches many homing bolts. Deals 50% more damage unless it's the first turn the target is in battle."ZThe user rocks out by using each Sound-based move they know. Only one use per battle."FThe user fires a dimensional mote, lowering the target's Sp. Def."QThe user meditates, raising both its Attack and Sp. Atk stats by four steps."\The user skillfully attacks around the enemy's guard. Can't miss and skips protections."jThe user slows the target's mind with a psychically infused blow. This has a 30% chance to frostbite."_Splits off a section of the target's psyche. Disables their last used move for five turns."kAstral energy explodes around the target. This move always goes first. The user also takes 50% recoil."KBy sacrificing half its max HP, the user makes the target fall asleep."^The user's HP is restored by 50% of the damage dealt. Power doubles if the foe is asleep."bSummons eclipse for six turns, boosting Psychic-type attacks and heralding the total eclipse."eThe user slashes the target with aura-enriched wings. This boosts