 Poké Ball that disables the Pokémon's last used move for 10 turns if it fails to catch it."dA remedial Poké Ball that restores the caught Pokémon's HP and eliminates any status problem.";A Poké Ball that makes caught Pokémon more friendly."`A comfortable Poké Ball that makes a caught wild Pokémon gain happiness twice as quickly."aA somewhat different Ball that becomes up to 4x better the more turns there are in a battle."aA somewhat different Poké Ball which has 3x strength on the first turn of a wild encounter."nA somewhat different Poké Ball that works better the lower the Pokémon's level is below your level cap."qA somewhat different Poké Ball that works at 3.5x strength on Pokémon species that were previously caught."CA Poké Ball whose strength varies with the Pokémon's weight."XA Poké Ball with 4x strength against Pokémon species with 100 or more base Speed."fA somewhat different Poké Ball that makes it easier to catch wild Pokémon while they're asleep."@A special Poké Ball with 5x strength against Ultra Beasts."bA somewhat rare Poké Ball that has been specially made to commemorate an event of some sort."eA quite rare Poké Ball that has been specially crafted to commemorate an occasion of some sort."TA ball whose striking appearance makes it popular despite its poor performance."hThe best Ball with the ultimate level of performance. It will catch any wild Pokémon without fail."pA ball with a mythical quality. It will catch any wild Pokémon without fail, and turn that Pokémon shiny."pThe Poke ball that contains Arceus. Unable to be replicated by humans, so how did you see this description."'A held item that can cure numbing."%A held item that can cure sleep."&A held item that can cure poison."$A held item that can cure burn.")A held item that can cure frostbite."%A held item that can cure dizzy."'A held item that can cure leeched."+A held item that can cure waterlogged."4A held item that can restore a move's PP by 10."2A held item that can cure any status probl