ns, exaggerating type matchups."QUpon switch out, lowers the foe's Attack and Sp. Atk stat by insulting them."OIts physical attacks go last but force the target to switch out after use."[On the first turn, its physical attacks trap the target and damage it for three turns.";Deals 30% more move damage to Pokémon slower than it."SRight before this Pokémon is attacked, the attacker's stat changes are reset."lThis Pokémon cannot enter the battle before Regidrago, Regice, Regirock, Registeel and Regieleki have."gWhile this Pokémon has an ally that isn't fully evolved, both Pokémon take 33% less move damage."/Deals 25% more damage per stockpile stack."xBoosts Sp. Def by 20%. When this Pokémon takes its second special hit from the same attacker, they become leeched."URaises this Pokémon's Sp. Atk by 50%, including Style Values and other bonuses."TRaises this Pokémon's Attack by 50%, including Style Values and other bonuses."aThis Pokémon's Dragon-type hits deal additional damage equal to half this Pokémon's level."2Has Light That Burns the Sky as its 5th move."^Upon entry, creates a Puzzle Room for four turns, swapping unmodified Attack and Sp. Atk."MBoth deals and takes double damage on its first full turn out in battle."=Releases a hazard layer of Spikes when hit by an attack.".Boosts power of light-based moves by 50%."NWhen this Pokémon is rampaging, it can choose the rampage moves it uses."pWhen this Pokémon is hit thrice, a Live Wire is set on the foe's side. The attacker hits itself in a rage."oProtects other allies, reducing their move damage taken by 33% while this Pokémon is using a status move."MLoses its Fire type. Whenever it uses a move, it gains that move's type."4Powers up Fairy-type moves by 50% in rainstorm."LIgnores screens, Substitute, and Abilities that would affect its moves."6On the first turn, its attacks poison the target."3Heals 1/8th HP every turn if hit by an attack."aLays an electrical hazard around the opponent when this Pokémon's HP is lowered below half."MBoosts the power of slice moves by 30%. They're twice as likely to crit."DTakes half damage from Dragon-, Fairy-, and Ghost-type attacks."KIf this Pokémon faints from Perish Song, it is revived in a new form."9Maximizes Sp. Atk when its HP is lowered below half."KAfter knocking out any Pokémon, regenerates its previously-used item."YLight moves change this Pokémon's secondary type and their power is boosted by 30%."-This Pokémon's moves heal for 25% more."IUpon entry during sunshine, heals the lowest HP ally or self by 33%."yPokémon that swap in for this have their non-volatile status conditions healed, and take 30% less damage that turn."IAt the end of each turn, heals from every volatile status condition."IBelow half health, it has a doubled crit chance and has +30% attack."zThis Pokémon can use Electric-type moves when recharging from an exhausting move, but cannot switch out during them."3Critical hits lower all of the victim's stats."zWhen this Pokémon is hit thrice, two layers of Spikes are set on the foe's side. The attacker will flinch next turn.":"Two to five" multi-hit moves hit an additional time.",Immune to Dark-type and Bug-type moves."@Spread moves hitting multiple targets deal 50% more damage."?Has a 30% chance to burn targets when using special moves."TWhen this Pokémon eats a Berry, it raises its Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps.":Heals 1/8th of its max HP each turn during sandstorm."_Immune to Rock-type moves and to Stealth Rock, and raises Speed whenever one would hit it."7While this Pokémon is active, Rooms do not decay.",Gets 50% more healing from all sources."-Makes foes unable to use priority moves."OImmune to Fighting-type and Rock-type moves. Prevents Stealth Rock damage."eProtected from random added effects. Takes 30% less damage from moves with random added effects.",All Pokémon deal 40% more move damage."FCan't be numbed, waterlogged, trapped, or have its Speed lowered."[Doubles critical hit chance for each Speed step up. All moves can random critical hit."OThis Pokémon is also Steel-type, but it takes 15% more damage from moves.""Doubles Defense in rainstorm.">Summons a sandstorm for four turns when hit by an attack."*Takes 30% less damage in a sandstorm."UWhen it attacks from underground in sandstorm, it'll transform into Reaper form."SBoosts this Pokémon's Speed by 50% in sandstorm. Can't miss during sandstorm."`During sandstorm, this Pokémon is twice as likely to crit and its Speed is boosted by 50%."9Special moves have a 30% chance to waterlog targets."vChanges the weather to Ring Eclipse, which heralds the total Ring Eclipse. Lingers for three turns after leaving."(Powers up Poison-type moves by 50%."EBoosts all of this Pokémon's move damage by 25% during eclipse."lWhen using a physical move, switch to Pirouette Forme. When using a special move, switch to Aria Forme."0Restores 1/4th health after any foe faints."OUpon entry during sandstorm, lowers foe's Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps."uAfter attacking the same foe twice, they become fractured, and a trap of levitating stones is set on their side."AMoves used against this Pokémon are disabled for two turns."sFoes that become burned are severely so. This Pokémon's Flying-type moves have a 30% chance to severely burn."MWhen targeted by a status move, the offending Pokémon becomes poisoned."6Special moves have a 30% chance to leech targets.",Foretelling moves deal 50% more damage."VBoosts one defending stat by two steps according to the foe's Attack and Sp. Atk."5Takes 25% less damage while using a status move."DBoosts Attack by 20% in hail, or 40% if also below half health."5Its attacks are critical against numbed targets."mDoubles the critical hit chance of random crit moves. This Pokémon's Speed is doubled while using them."6Its physical attacks reduce the target's Defense."OImmune to Steel-type moves and boosts Defense and Sp. Def when hit by one."\Punching moves change this Pokémon's secondary type and their power is boosted by 