Keep it up!"\w[]\wm\c[12]\l[3]You returned to {1} with your Pokémon, hoping to quickly come up with a strategy to defeat the Gym Leader..."xTurns to Finale Form when only unfainted on team. Ignores the condition of a perfect battle if it isn't in a pinch."]Raises Speed by four steps when its HP is lowered below half. Moves next when being hit."HWhen this Pokémon eats a Berry, it restores 25% of its max health.">Raises Attack by 2 steps after knocking out any Pokémon."�Upon entry, spreads poisonous dust which poisons any Pokémon stay in for 2 turns. When any Pokémon are poisoned, boosts Defense by 2 steps."CHalves move damage dealt or taken when HP is greater than 50%."LIt changes secondary type to that of the dance moves it's about to use."EHeals 1/8th HP in rainstorm, 1/4th when hit by Water-type moves."WDeals 50% more damage to targets who have already taken damage or moved this turn."SUpon entry, creates an Emotion Room for 4 turns, adding an ability every turn."PUpon entry, this Pokémon heals itself for 1/5th max HP. This can overheal."CHeals 1/8th HP in sunshine, 1/4th when hit by Fire-type moves."?Raises Sp. Atk by 2 steps after knocking out any Pokémon."sEach turn, raises Speed by 4 steps and loses 1/8th max HP. If Speed was maxed, instead Speed and HP are reset."RComes out disguised as a Pokémon in back. Reduces damage by 30% in disguise."iRaises Speed by four steps when a stat is lowered by a foe. Makes foes unable to use priority moves."@Uses Wish when hit by an attack or knocks out any Pokémon."rPokémon can't raise their stats. Pokémon that use dance or sound moves take damage equal to 1/4th their HP."UHeals all non-volatile status conditions and 10% of max HP when it switches out."rAfter knocking out any Pokémon/being knocked out, raises/lowers its/attacker's Sp. Atk and Speed by 2 steps."lAfter fainting from exploding, revives after five turns, but requires above 50% HP if caused by others."0Copies opponents' species' legal Abilities."[This Pokémon r