Z: MENU"Terrain Tag:"FTo ensure that the changes remain, close and reopen RPG Maker XP."Set the terrain tag."$Welcome to the Battle Monument."'Take the singles battle challenge?"Please come this way."0Your party is not legal for this challenge."The match will now begin!"Let me heal your party."%Congratulations on your victory!"Thanks for playing."Better luck next time."Come back another time."Battle Monument Team {1}"H\me[Earn battle points]\ptYou've earned {1} battle points.\wtnp[70]"'Welcome to the battle points shop!"Choose a battle."#Number of rounds is 0 or less."RENTAL POKéMON"POKéMON SWAP"Select Pokémon to swap."{1} - {2} Pokémon"Choose the first Pokémon." Choose the second Pokémon."Choose the third Pokémon."PKMN FOR SWAP"Select Pokémon to accept."SUMMARY"DESELECT"	RENT"OTHERS"!Are these three Pokémon OK?"	SWAP"RECHOOSE"Accept this Pokémon?"Quit swapping?" Preparing to generate teams""Generating teams ({1} of {2})"$Simulating battles ({1} of {2})"Writing results"0Generate Pokémon teams for this challenge?"NO"YES, USE EXISTING"YES, USE NEW"YES"Choose a challenge."8This challenge will use the Pokémon list from {1}."-This may take a long time. Are you sure?"Team generation complete."Here I come!"Yes, I won!"Man, I lost!"No identical nicknames."9Sorry, you can only have {1} legendary on your team!"'Pokémon must be the same species."(Pokémon can't be the same species."$The combined levels exceed {1}."No identical hold items."{1} Pokémon are needed."{1} is not allowed."This team is not allowed."Standard Cup"Double Cup"Fancy Cup"Little Cup"Light Cup"SIt's open to a battling guide written by someone with the username "apolLyon.""1.1 Roles/Cores"2.1 Leads"3.2 Hazards"(Which entry would you like to read?"KEverything on your team needs a point. Every Pokémon needs a purpose."PIf you can't sum up its role on your team in a sentence, keep it in the PC."TEvery bit of that Pokémon should reinforce its role. Moves, items, everything."@All six Pokémon on your team need a role, narrow or broad."=Two Pokémon with synergistic roles are called a "core.""\If the two of them can take hits from a whole bunch of things, that's a defensive core."nIf together they threaten lots of Pokémon and deal with each others' counters, that's an offensive core."SCombine both and you have a balanced core. Good cores make for powerful teams."QYou don't need them, but they're a surefire way to give your team some bite."8The Pokémon you start a fight with is your "lead.""OStart every fight with it and it's a "dedicated lead." Make it a good one."@Its job is to kick things off in your favor from round one."dUsually that's by vomiting up a whole bunch of hazards. Sometimes it sets screens and explodes."kA few just try to delete whatever's on the other side, usually with short-term power boosts like Gems."FSpeaking of which, your opponent is going to have their own lead."AStop it. Taunt it, put it to sleep, or put it in the ground."IThe arena is going to very rapidly fill up with nasty pointy things."�That's because wasting a turn setting them up in the short term pays off big in the long term when they chew up a few Pokémon worth of health over the course of the match."tIf you like being alive, pack something that can clean up hazards – Defog, Terraform, or Rapid Spin, usually."uStealth Rocks are the most common hazard, so prioritize hazard removal if you've got lots of Rock-weak Pokémon."�Remember: if your favorite little gremlin is switching out nine times a match or is cripplingly weak to funny pebbles, put Heavy-Duty Boots on it." They're cute and effective."You exit the PC."VIt's open to a battling guide written by someone with the username "snowwhip401.""Even keel"Best foot forward"Rolling with the punches"<All the little pieces of your team need their own role."dUse whatever you want; just ensure that it's got something to do and the best odds of doing it."5Give bulky Pokémon Leftovers and healing moves."IGive strong, slow Pokémon Focus Sashes, Vests, or ways to speed up."You get the idea."aIf you can, try to have all kinds of Pokémon on your team, so you have answers to anything."pPhysical and special bulk and power, type matchups, speed profiles – a diverse team is a diverse toolbox."ISend out the Pokémon that helps everything else on your team first.":If you have a weather or a Room to set up, get to it."EIf you don't have a clear, clean gameplan, ruin your opponent's."wA dedicated lead's worst fear is usually a strong multi-hitting move. Neither Sturdy nor Sash can help them there."}As opposed to simply trading hazards, outspeeding and KOing a lead before it gets going can give you an early advantage."8Each Pokémon's utility is defined by the opponent."ZIf your opponent has several Fire-type Pokémon, your Primarina is far more valuable."0Conserve its health and leverage its power."]In the same match, an Aegislash may be far less valuable – be willing to sacrifice it."ZThere's no shame in letting a Pokémon fall in order to get a safe switch to another."xWhile they may seem drastic, moves such as Healing Wish or Explosion can turn the tide of a match in a single turn."kFainting the user can, if used with finesse, be an advantage – think of them as the ultimate U-Turn."8The blizzard is too strong! You cannot go this way!",The Corviknight stares at you intently."<You get the sense that you've failed some sort of test."Green-thumbed"Savior"Scornful"Grand Design"Treason".<i>Drink the regal blood if you must.</i>"C<i>Indulge in your <b>traitorous nature</b> if you insist.</i>"<i>Repulsive flea...</i>"0<i><b>I will swat you from the sky.</b></i>"7<i>Let this act as a lesson in humility, worm!</i>"<i>What!!?</i>"!<i>How... how could you?</i>"T<i>To think!! My gift to the world, in the hands of the <b>undeserving</b>!</i>"d<i>Insolent fool! Treasonous wretch!!! Usurping the King of All in your desperate attemp–</i>"MCalyrex's protests fade away, leaving an echoing silence in its absence."#I'm energized and ready to go!"ZI don't spend my energy needlessly. Grab me a Sweet Heart and I'll consider battling."So, you got one?"FWow, you actually did it. With this much energy, I'm unstoppable!"?It's much too cold in here to battle without a pick-me-up."HThey're the Skeevee Eevee specialty. Where? East side of town, duh!"#Witness my brilliant battling!"ZMinerals are great reference material. You wouldn't happen to have, say, an Eviolite?"2It's quite obscure, so...please part with it."@Ahh...spectacular. I hope this battle is just as beautiful!"U...shading like this, coloring like that... sorry, what? Did you need something?"QNo? Well, they're quite rare. Perhaps Emma offers them...just north of here.".Style and substance are one and the same!"ZCompared to Noel, my fashion is lacking. But with a Ninja Scarf, I'd stand right out!"4Could I gently request one from you... perhaps?"OTo express my gratitude, we shall battle. A chance to show off your style!"OMy reputation lies in tatters. How will I ever live up to Noel's standard?"ZI heard a rumor that they're being sold in Prizca Castle. A man by the name of Diego."!It's time to bring you down!"LHauling sculptures is too hard. It'd be much easier with a Float Stone."Got one on hand?"9Efficient! There'll be time enough for a battle now!"ASorry, but I won't be able to battle if I throw out my back!"fYou don't have one. Well, Nature's Gallery will have them in stock. That's two shops to the east."7I'm skilled in everything. That includes battling!"MYou look ready to help me find a Knight Helmet. Don't ask why I need it."So, cough it up."%My safety comes first. En garde!"EDon't you know who I am? I can't keep risking my head every day!"_Tch, don't have one? They sell them in the castle courtyard. Diego's something or another."L\wm<i>The mention of a certain someone manifests a ball of light...</i>"D\wm<i>You get the sense that you've collected enough light.</i>"0\wm<i>Your friend will be very pleased.</i>"4\wm<i>You should visit her very nice house.</i>"?\wm<i>She is waiting for you <imp>near Velenz</imp>...</i>"Q\wm<i>You get the sense that you've found about half the light you need.</i>"8\wm<i>Your friend is waiting with anticipation.</i>"(\wm<i>Continue your collection.</i>"J\wm<i>A <imp>vision of golden light</imp> appears in your mind...</i>"\wm\ss<i>{1}</i>"+A tattered notebook sits on the table."!It's titled "Tapu Log Book.""Notes: Cruel Cocoon"Notes: Turbulent Sky"Notes: Primal Forest"Notes: Misdirecting Fog"Stop Reading"*Which section would you like to read?"~Tapu Lele's ability "Flutter Totem" creates a "Cruel Cocoon" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."UAt the end of each turn, it heals Pokémon on its side by 1/8th of their max HP."IHowever, they also lose 1 PP from each of their moves. Cruel indeed."}Tapu Koko's ability "Storm Totem" creates a "Turbulent Sky" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."�Pokémon on its side get a 30% move damage boost, but they are prevented from using moves that are the same type as the move they most recently used."SOr, to state it another way, they can't use the same move type twice in a row."|Tapu Bulu's ability "Wild Totem" creates a "Primal Forest" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."WWhenever a Pokémon on its side is hit by an offensive attack, it becomes enraged."jThereby, its defense stats are both lowered by 1 step and its attack stats are both raised by 1 step."~Tapu Fini's ability "Fog Totem" creates a "Misdirecting Fog" upon entry that only affects its side and lasts for 6 turns."nWhenever a foe finishes attacking a Pokémon on its side, the attacker is forced to switch out of battle."wUnlike moves such as Roar or Whirlwind, however, the trainer has enough time to select the replacement themselves."You put down the book."Leave it."Punch it!"Kick it!"Hug it?""A hanging bag. Give it a hit?""You decide to leave it alone."7Your fist makes a satisfying thud against the bag."Oww, you hurt your wrist!"GYou thrust your hips at the right time, and send the
bag swinging!"5You swing your leg at the bag, to little effect."You hug the bag."4You get some strange looks from around the gym."%A {1} emerged from the wormhole!"7Think you can handle whatever strategy I'm hiding?"5Ah, my dear friend \PN, care for another battle?"<Hey there, \PN! How about a friendly Pokémon showdown?"HThe time has come for us to engage in yet another thrilling battle!"EGreetings, esteemed champion! Fancy a clash of Pokémon prowess?"F\PN, my rival, I humbly request your presence on the battlefield."YThe stage is set, and my new team is eager to take you by surprise. Shall we battle?"J\PN, the champion of Makya, a challenger awaits you. Will you accept?"(The thrill of surprise is imminent!"MHark! Brace yourself for a battle of wonder, where victory is uncertain!"QWell, well, well! Fancy a sparring session, with a dash of unpredictability?"HHey, you! Up for a surprise Pokémon battle? Or are you too scared?">Champion, huh? You got the gumption to face my surprises?"OGet ready to unravel the enigma of my team. Will it be a treat or a trick?"ZWarning! Battling me may cause trembling, excessive sweating, and a memorable defeat."TNo point in saying much. I've come to expect this sort of performance from you."CHaha, you got me this time! But I'll be back with a vengeance!"VYou've mastered the art of surprise attacks! I bow down to your wacky brilliance."NMy perfectionism failed me. But if I can just perfect my perfectionism..."YUtterly defeated... I'm at a loss for words. I'll need to find some new inspiration.":\PN, you really knows how to bring out my weaknesses."\Defeated, but at least I can pursue my dream of becoming a professional pillow fighter."FMy Pokémon must have been practicing their synchronized failing."FI'll try to laugh about that loss. It's the best medicine, right?"@Well, at least I'll be known for being a unique individual."WI must confess, you're like a puzzle I just can't solve. Kudos for the mind games!"4Ouch! That defeat hit harder than a Hyper Beam."eDefeat stings like a Poison Jab to the heart. Time to reevaluate my strategy and lick my wounds."MYou've shown me the true meaning of humiliation. Frankly, it does stink.".....dang."9Sometimes I regret deciding to never use held items."QThe surprise play must have worked, since I took some of yours down with me!">Oh, well, my perfect plan went awry. Time to recalculate."WDefeat? No worries, I'll just add it to my collection of almost-perfect victories!"WBravo! Your team concoction was like a spicy curry that set my taste buds on fire."8\PN, your battles are a roller coaster of emotions."LSometimes even the best fall short. I'll dust myself off and try again!",Looks like you're still a worthy rival!"GWell, that was a close call! My heart was pounding with each move."]I gave it my all, but luck wasn't on my side. At least I'm gonna blame that one on luck."TA loss? How unexpected! It's not like I meticulously planned for this scenario."$Well, at least I lost in style."KHats off to you, my friend. You battled like a true Pokémon virtuoso."9Bravo! Your battle strategy was truly a work of art."RAh, my dear Pokémon, we were so close to achieving flawless victory. Alas..."[Congratulations, \PN! You've proven that even the best can be outshone... temporarily."ZOh, look! A defeat. Just what I needed to keep my ego in check. Thanks for that, \PN."${1} hands you a pouch of candy."BCannot set the chosen NPC1 to be the same as the chosen NPC2."BCannot set the chosen NPC2 to be the same as the chosen NPC1."nError: should not be able to change which NPC's have been chosen for randomization outside of debug mode."lThe submitted NPC ID could not be made traitor as it was not randomly selected on this playthrough: {1}"<This is a recoverable error. Please alert a programmer."Set NPC1 Chosen":Set which NPC was chosen for NPC Randomization slot 1"DChoose which NPC ID you would like to have be the selected one."Set NPC2 Chosen":Set which NPC was chosen for NPC Randomization slot 2"a\wm\ss\l[2]Beyond this door, a <imp>Crimson Mask</imp> and a <imp>Teal Mask</imp> await you."G\wm\ss\l[2]Beyond this door, a <imp>Crimson Mask</imp> awaits you."D\wm\ss\l[2]Beyond this door, a <imp>Teal Mask</imp> awaits you."R\wm\ss\l[2]If you continue, reconciliation will <imp>become impossible</imp>.""Enter through the black door?"DCan't warp to any shards because they're all collected already!"0\wmThe words of a poem appear in your mind.",\ss\wm"Watchful eye, a towering sight.""-\ss\wm"Budding hope, with 3-fold might.""&\ss\wm"We await you, o slayer...""#Was this an attempt at a gaff?"%Prank the dottering old man, eh?"(I've not gone blind yet, fledgling!">Error! Could not determine how to revive the given stone."KI have never been more overcome with emotion than in this very moment."It's beautiful."Here, take it."CAll I ask is that you appreciate it for many years, young one."C\i[SPANNINGBAND]What? The Spanning Bands are suddenly glowing!"H\i[SPANNINGBAND]They glow in sync with the <imp>Avatar Totem</imp>."G\i[SPANNINGBAND]A vision of Casaba Villa flashes across your mind."U\i[SPANNINGBAND]You sense that some sort of <imp>connection</imp> has been made."Makyan Champion"/\wmThe victor is \PN!\me[Bug catching 1st]"LThe game has been updated, you must take on the challenge from scratch!"7The waiting room for tournament entrants is ahead."qOnce you enter, you will not be able to interact with your team in any way until the tournament is complete."_This means swapping Pokemon, moves, abilities, or items, or even changing your team order."?A nurse is provided, however, for healing between matches."$Enter and begin the tournament?"YIf you leave, the tournament will be reset and your progress within it will be lost."2Would you still like to leave the tournament?"!{1} awaits you in the arena."Are you ready to battle?"6Ok, let me know when you are ready to battle {1}.")Your next match will be against {1}."/Return to me when you are ready to battle."5\wmThe match between {1} and \PN will now begin!"LOdds are displayed for the grand final, gathered from a spectator poll."KOnly 20 percent of respondents expect you to win against your brother."
